Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.76,0:00:04.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello.\N你好。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.30,0:00:04.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello.\N你好。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.83,0:00:07.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow, this crowd looks amazing.\N哇，这个观众群体看起来太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.16,0:00:12.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, as Madison just said, my name is Tiffany Janzen and I'm going to be your moderator today.\N嗯，正如麦迪逊刚才所说，我叫蒂芙尼·詹森，今天由我来担任本次圆桌讨论的主持人。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.94,0:00:16.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,A little bit about me, I am the founder of Tiffen Tech.\N简单介绍一下我自己，我是Tiffen Tech的创始人。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.22,0:00:21.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I don't know about you, but I have been counting down the days for this panel.\N我不知道你们怎么样，但我一直在倒数，期待这场圆桌讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.97,0:00:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Humanoids have been in the the they we've seen a lot of advancements with them very recently and to\N人形机器人最近我们看到了很多进展，它们已经进入了我们的视野。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.08,0:00:35.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,be able to sit down with some of the leaders in this space and hear from them is truly incredible.\N能够与这一领域的几位领军者坐在一起，亲耳聆听他们的分享，真的令人难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.34,0:00:38.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only to learn where we are now but where we are headed.\N不仅能了解我们目前所处的位置，还能看清未来的方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.67,0:00:41.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's start with a round of introductions.\N我们先从自我介绍开始吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.27,0:00:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll start with Burnt.\N我先从伯恩特开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.72,0:00:43.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.06,0:00:44.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,So my name is Burnt Barnick.\N我叫伯恩特·巴尼克。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.73,0:00:52.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the founder and CEO of 1X and we're on a mission to create an abundance of labor through these safe\N我是 1X 的创始人兼首席执行官，我们的使命是通过这些安全、智能的人形机器人创造丰富的劳动力。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.20,0:01:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,intelligent humanoids and we really believe that to truly get to intelligence these robots they need to live and learn among us.\N我们坚信，要真正实现智能，这些机器人必须与我们共同生活、共同学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.76,0:01:08.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why we think consumer has to happen first to really be able to ex to experience all of the\N正因为如此，我们认为消费级应用必须先行，才能真正体验到人类生活的种种细微差别。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.62,0:01:15.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,nuances that is kind of human life and then use that intelligence to be able to do useful labor in all other\N然后利用这种智能，去实现其他所有领域的有用劳动。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.44,0:01:26.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,verticals down the line right hospitals elderly care retail factories logistics it's exciting y hi I am Deepak Pathak and I'm\N比如医院、老年护理、零售、工厂、物流，这令人兴奋。嗨，我是迪帕克·帕塔克，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.14,0:01:32.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,CEO and co-founder of skilled AI at skilled what we are doing is we are building a general brain for robotics ICS.\N我是 Skilled AI 的首席执行官兼联合创始人，\N在 Skilled AI，我们正在为机器人打造一个通用大脑。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.12,0:01:39.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our thesis is that we can have a single shared model because robotics is a field which is anyway scarce of data.\N我们的观点是，我们可以使用一个共享的统一模型，因为机器人领域本身数据就非常稀缺。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.12,0:01:43.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,We might as well use everything that we available from any platform, any task, any scenarios.\N我们不妨利用来自任何平台、任何任务、任何场景的所有可用数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.53,0:01:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So think of it as like a large scale foundation model you can use for any robot, any hardware, any task, any scenarios.\N所以你可以把它想象成一个大规模的基础模型，适用于任何机器人、任何硬件、任何任务、任何场景。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.72,0:01:55.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh Pras Velagapudi, the CTO at Agility Robotics and at Agility,\N普拉斯·维拉加普迪，Agility Robotics 的首席技术官，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.41,0:02:02.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,our humanoid digit is made for work and we're bringing it out to manufacturing and logistics use cases today.\N我们的仿人机器人专为工作而生，今天我们将它推向制造和物流的应用场景。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.31,0:02:10.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,We feel that the best way to get the technology out there and learn from it is to be able to get real customers and real deployments doing work.\N我们认为，将这项技术推广出去并从中学习的最佳方式，\N就是能够获得真实客户和真实部署，让机器人真正投入工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.65,0:02:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's what we've been focused on and getting a robot out there and in the workforce.\N这正是我们一直专注的方向，也是我们把机器人推向市场并融入劳动力的过程。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.40,0:02:21.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, Aaron Saunders, CTO of Boston Dynamics, uh, been working on humanoids before they were cool.\N嗯，波士顿动力公司的首席技术官亚伦·桑德斯，早在人形机器人流行之前就一直在研究这类技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.46,0:02:26.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and at Boston, you know, our mission has been, uh, um, the same for a long time.\N嗯，在波士顿动力，我们的使命长期以来一直如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.67,0:02:27.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's to make robots real.\N就是让机器人真正变得现实可用。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.85,0:02:30.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and we've shipped a couple thousand robots.\N我们已经交付了数千台机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.26,0:02:33.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,The humanoid is the the latest, uh, kind of announcement for us.\N人形机器人是我们最近发布的一项重要消息。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.41,0:02:39.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, and we're really wanting to bring a product to market that, uh, can do real useful work, right?\N我们非常希望推出一款真正能完成有用工作的产品，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.57,0:02:44.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, to do work that, uh, um, uh, removes people from dirty, dull, dangerous things.\N也就是能够替代人类从事肮脏、枯燥、危险的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.44,0:02:47.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's the thing that we've been up to uh for a long time and\N这正是我们长期致力于的方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.31,0:02:50.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think there's more work to do yet but we're pretty excited about where we're going.\N我认为还有更多工作要做，但我们对未来的方向感到非常兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.97,0:02:52.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi everyone, I'm Jim Fan.\N大家好，我是范麟熙。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.64,0:02:57.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I'm the co-lead of NVIDIA GEAR Lab and also project is GR00T.\N嗯，我是英伟达 GEAR 实验室的联合负责人，同时也是 GR00T 项目负责人。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.52,0:03:04.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh GR00T is NVIDIA's moonshot initiative at building u the foundation model the robot brain for\N嗯，GR00T 是英伟达在构建人形机器人基础模型——机器人大脑方面的登月计划。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.24,0:03:11.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,humanoid robots and GR00T also represents our strategy for the next generation computing platform for physical AI.\NGR00T 也代表了我们为物理 AI 所打造的下一代计算平台的战略。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.19,0:03:14.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're also on a mission to democratize physical AI.\N我们还致力于让物理 AI 实现普及化。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.54,0:03:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, yesterday at Jensen's uh keynote, we announced open sourcing of the GR00T N1 model,\N事实上，昨天在黄仁勋的主题演讲中，我们宣布了 GR00T N1 模型的开源。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.16,0:03:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh which is the world's first open humanoid robot foundation model.\N这是全球首个开源的人形机器人基础模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.84,0:03:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's only two billion parameters and um it punches above its weights.\N它仅有二十亿参数，但表现远超其规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.72,0:03:37.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You are basically holding the world's state-of-the-art autonomous humanoid intelligence in the palm of your hand.\N你实际上正将全球最先进的自主人形机器人智能握在掌心。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.84,0:03:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and um I would also like to say that um just like everyone else on this panel um I started working robotics before it was sexy.\N嗯，我也想说，和本场 panel 上的其他人一样，我早在人形机器人还不热门时就开始从事相关工作了。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.72,0:03:49.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and today I see the full house here.\N嗯，今天这里座无虚席。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.76,0:03:52.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I'm just really really glad that they become sexy today.\N所以我真的很高兴，它们如今终于变得热门了。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.80,0:03:53.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So thank you all so much.\N非常感谢大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.86,0:04:00.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of you made my day.\N你们所有人让我的一天变得完美。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.80,0:04:02.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank you all for being here.\N哦，感谢大家的到来。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.06,0:04:04.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know we're all excited.\N我知道我们都很激动。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.24,0:04:12.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had a call before our panel obviously and in that conversation I can't recall who exactly it was but someone\N我们显然在小组讨论前有过一次通话，在那次对话中，我记不清具体是谁了，但有人提到
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.21,0:04:22.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,shared on the call that robotics is the oldest application of AI and historically it's moved the slowest not the case\N机器人技术是人工智能最古老的应用，历史上它进展最慢，但现在已不再是这样了。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.22,0:04:28.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,anymore I would say and what has changed I think I I raised that question in that call yeah so um\N我认为，变化的关键在于，我在这次通话中提出了这个问题，是的，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.71,0:04:37.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,well I think the biggest change is Jensen now is paying attention to robotics Jensen's got a Jensen's got a Midas touch,\N我觉得最大的变化是，黄仁勋现在开始关注机器人技术了。黄仁勋有“点石成金”的能力，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.19,0:04:37.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.58,0:04:41.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Any field he puts his finger on is going to scale exponentially.\N他涉足的任何领域都会实现指数级增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.46,0:04:44.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we call Jensen scaling law, right?\N我们称之为黄仁勋的缩放定律，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.34,0:04:46.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,So jokes aside,\N说笑归说笑，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.13,0:04:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think uh robotics one of the oldest field as long as AI itself existed and the reason that robotics is so hard um is because the Moravex paradox.\N我认为，机器人技术是人工智能诞生以来最古老的领域之一，\N而机器人技术之所以如此困难，其原因在于莫拉维克悖论。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.80,0:05:05.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what this paradox says is the things that are easy for humans are actually really hard for machines and vice versa right the things\N这个悖论的意思是，人类容易的事情对机器来说实际上非常困难，反之亦然。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.12,0:05:12.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we kind of u find extremely hard like creative writing may actually not be that hard for machines and that's why the LMS like the\N我们觉得极其困难的事情，比如创意写作，对机器来说可能并不那么难，\N这就是为什么如今自然语言处理和计算机视觉的进展远超机器人技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.45,0:05:21.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,NLP right computer vision is being solved much better than robotics these days so we are facing this paradox right now and now what has changed\N我们正面临这一悖论，而如今情况发生了变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.20,0:05:31.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say a couple of aspects one is uh on the model side um because of large foundation models like Loom's the Chach GPT moment.\N我认为有几个方面发生了改变，首先是模型层面，\N由于像 Loom 和 ChatGPT 这样的大型基础模型的出现。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.50,0:05:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we have models that can do reasoning and we have multimodal models that understands computer vision\N现在我们有了具备推理能力的模型，还有能理解计算机视觉的多模态模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.76,0:05:43.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,right open vocabulary understanding of the 3D visual world much much better than what we had before\N它们对三维视觉世界的开放词汇理解，远比以前更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.84,0:05:49.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,and these are necessary but insufficient conditions to solve robotics like you got to solve vision uh\N这些是解决机器人技术所必需的条件，但还不够，你必须先解决视觉问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.77,0:05:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,to have a really good vision system before you even talk about having a general purpose robot.\N在谈论通用机器人之前，你必须先拥有一个非常出色的视觉系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.96,0:06:01.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think the rest of models are becoming really really good that we can start to tackle robotics uh a lot more systematically.\N我认为，现在模型已经变得足够好，我们可以更系统地着手解决机器人技术问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.01,0:06:07.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's number one and number two what has changed is uh on the data side.\N这是第一点，第二点是数据层面的变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.14,0:06:15.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you know unlike Loom and I'm quoting Ilia Sask here he says the internet is the fossil fuel right for AI.\N你知道，不像 Loom，我引用伊利亚·萨斯的话：互联网是 AI 的化石燃料。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.21,0:06:23.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh well robotics doesn't even have the fossil fuel at least for LMS you can download text you can scrape text from Wikipedia.\N但机器人技术甚至还没有这样的化石燃料，至少对于语言模型来说，\N你可以下载文本，也可以从维基百科抓取文本。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.62,0:06:26.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where do we scrape motor control?\N我们从哪里获取电机控制的数据？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.14,0:06:30.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where do we scrape uh all of those like robot trajectories from the internet?\N我们从互联网上哪里获取那些机器人轨迹数据？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.31,0:06:31.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't find it anywhere.\N你根本找不到这些数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.84,0:06:33.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we got to generate data.\N所以我们必须生成数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.45,0:06:35.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got to collect data at scale.\N我们必须大规模收集数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.42,0:06:43.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think the advent uh of simulation of GPU accelerated simulation really makes these problems more tractable because\N我认为 GPU 加速仿真技术的出现，真正让这些问题变得可解决，因为
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.44,0:06:50.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,now you can generate like 10 years worth of training data in maybe three hours worth of compute time.\N现在你可以在大约三小时的计算时间内生成相当于十年的训练数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.27,0:06:54.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that really takes us beyond this data paradox.\N这真正让我们摆脱了数据悖论。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.15,0:07:00.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's number two and number three is on hardware side and we have uh some of the most extraordinary uh founders on\N这是第二点，第三点是硬件方面，我们拥有
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.97,0:07:06.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of the best um robot hardware we have ever seen and I think hardware has become a lot better and also a\N一些最杰出的创始人，以及我们见过的最优秀的机器人硬件，我认为硬件不仅变得更好了，也
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.02,0:07:14.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,lot cheaper right like like this year we have seen hardware um in range of maybe 40k that's the price of a car\N便宜了很多，比如今年我们看到的硬件价格大约在 4 万美元左右，相当于一辆汽车的价格。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.90,0:07:24.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and back in 2001 NASA built Robonaut one of the first major humanoids and it's like $1.5 million in 2001 USD Right.\N而在 2001 年，NASA 建造了第一个重要的类人机器人 Robonaut，\N当时花费了 150 万美元（2001 年美元）。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.09,0:07:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's finally become becoming affordable that um uh it will become mainstream very quickly.\N所以，它终于变得负担得起，很快就会成为主流。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.60,0:07:33.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Erin, I'd love to hear from you on this.\N埃琳，我很想听听你的看法。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.20,0:07:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You in your intro, you mentioned you've you were in robotics before it was cool.\N你在介绍中提到，你在机器人领域变得热门之前就已涉足。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.80,0:07:38.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what do you think has changed?\N那么，你认为有什么变化？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.51,0:07:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think um that was a a lot of terrain.\N是的，我认为那是一片广阔的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.12,0:07:44.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, let me try to pick away at some some some pieces there.\N那让我试着分析一下其中的一些要点。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.48,0:07:49.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I do think the the kind of closure of the sim tore gap is a big deal, right?\N我认为仿真与现实之间的差距缩小是一个重大进展，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.45,0:07:54.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think for a long time uh the robotics community kind of struggled with\N所以，长期以来，机器人社区一直面临困扰，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.45,0:08:00.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,creating a uh um a simulation environment that represented physics properly and that was computationally efficient.\N即创建一个能准确体现物理规律且计算高效的仿真环境。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.00,0:08:01.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.28,0:08:05.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we could create very complex models that did a very good job of representing\N我们可以构建非常复杂的模型，很好地模拟
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.75,0:08:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,the physical world but we couldn't run them at real time or faster than real time.\N物理世界，但无法以实时或更快的速度运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.52,0:08:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think for me the the biggest change has probably been the ability to\N所以我认为对我而言，最大的变化可能就是能够以超过实时的速度来模拟现实世界的物理规律，\N这让我们能够加速探索更多仿真，也能利用这些仿真来开发新的AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.60,0:08:18.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,represent the physics of the real world in greater than real time which lets you accelerate\N然后你知道，许多零散组件的标准化和普及化。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.17,0:08:22.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,how many simulations you can explore and how you can use those simulations to develop\N所以我认为我们可能需要给一些相邻行业极大的肯定。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.76,0:08:27.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,new AI and then you know the the the commoditization of so many bits and pieces.\N比如消费电子行业，已经发展出电池和摄像头，这些技术让感知、观察世界和计算成为可能。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.05,0:08:31.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think we we probably need to give a huge amount of credit to some adjacent industries right.\N当我回望过去，甚至10到15年前，大多数机器人还布满了电路板和电线，电池容量非常小。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.86,0:08:37.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,So consumer electronics have developed batteries and cameras that that that like\N这种情况已经完全改变了，我们现在可以放入大量计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.22,0:08:42.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know the the technology for perception for seeing the world for computing.\N我们可以放入微型传感器，它们功耗很低，因此。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.12,0:08:51.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh when I look back you know even 101 15 years you know most of the robot was full of PCBAs and wires and had a very small amount\N我认为组件的标准化是关键，我不认为这主要在于低成本，虽然现在这确实是个重点。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.62,0:08:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,of battery capacity and that's completely changed right we can put a huge amount\N但我觉得我们正迎来机器人初创企业的时代，正是因为全球供应链的成熟。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.40,0:08:59.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,of compute in we can put tiny sensors in uh they're power efficient so I\N有了这些，我们才能实现真正的突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.75,0:09:06.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,think the commoditization of the the components and I don't think it's so much about low cost I know that's a big focus right now but I think the\N以前的机器人几乎全是电路板和线缆，电池容量极小。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.98,0:09:11.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,reason we're seeing the era of the robotic startup is because there's a global supply\N现在我们能放入大量计算能力，也能塞进微型传感器，它们功耗低，效率高。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.36,0:09:15.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,chain full of really important pieces that you can put together as a puzzle piece.\N一整串非常重要的组件，你可以像拼图一样将它们组合起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.18,0:09:21.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we've elevated the robotics community from the people trying to design every cog to people who\N因此我们已将机器人社区从那些试图设计每一个齿轮的人，提升到了能够像拼图一样组合这些部件的人。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.58,0:09:26.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,can put those things together as a puzzle and you and and basically be operated at a higher level.\N你们可以这样操作，基本上在更高层次上运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.62,0:09:31.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now we have companies that are operating at the intelligence level that are developing applications\N现在我们有了在智能层面运作的公司，它们正在开发应用，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.27,0:09:36.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,rather than spending all that same amount of capital and energy just making a physical machine stand.\N而不是花费同样多的资金和精力，仅仅为了制造一台能站立的物理机器。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.96,0:09:37.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.57,0:09:37.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.98,0:09:46.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can add something to I think what Jim's point initially uh about uh I think you put it very well about all the differences that have changed.\N我想补充一点，我认为吉姆最初提到的观点——关于所有变化的差异，你表达得非常到位。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.26,0:09:49.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I want to add that AI was not just the first application.\N我想补充的是，AI 并不只是第一个应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.02,0:09:53.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sorry, robotics was not the first application of AI, it is what AI is like.\N抱歉，机器人并不是 AI 的第一个应用，它正是 AI 的本质所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.85,0:09:58.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you look at the original documents of Turing when he talked about AI, it was for robotics.\N如果你看看图灵最初关于 AI 的文档，他讨论的正是机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.29,0:10:06.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was like you should make something that learn instead of building like an adult make something that learns like a child and then it can grow.\N他的意思是，你应该制造一种能学习的东西，而不是像造一个成年人那样，\N而是造一个像孩子一样能学习的东西，然后它就能成长。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.08,0:10:09.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can put the same robot in a classroom it will grow to be adult over time.\N你可以把同一个机器人放进教室，它会随着时间逐渐成长成一个成年人。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.69,0:10:18.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a fascinating thought and he had this thought in 1950s right because language vision all of these things are cool but if you look\N这是一个引人入胜的想法，他在20世纪50年代就有了这个想法，\N因为语言、视觉等所有这些都很酷，但如果你观察自然发展的时间线就会发现，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.38,0:10:26.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,at the nature they come much later in timeline compared to physical action like for instance LLMs we are training on the data it's from\N它们出现的时间远晚于物理动作。比如大型语言模型，我们训练的数据来自
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.93,0:10:33.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe last 100 years 200 years let's say thousand we are not training more than thousand years of data humans have been around for more\N大约过去100到200年，就算说上千年，我们训练的数据也远不到千年。人类已经存在了超过千年，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.40,0:10:37.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,than thousand years so it's not that language led to intelligence it\N所以并不是语言导致了智能，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.51,0:10:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,was the infrastructure already existed Our brain actually existed which came through physical\N而是基础设施早已存在。我们的大脑实际上已经存在，它源于物理推理，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.92,0:10:49.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,reasoning which is why the impact is so big like if you you don't have to explain a person to any person what robotics is\N这也正是为什么影响如此巨大的原因——比如你不需要向任何人解释什么是机器人技术，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.21,0:10:57.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can feel it because we do physical task every other day every company gets impacted by robotics and that's the main deal so what\N你能够切身感受到，因为我们每天都在做物理任务，\N每家公司都会受到机器人技术的影响，这才是关键所在。那么，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.42,0:11:04.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,has changed apart from all the factors that Jim mentioned like these are technical details that is yes but what has changed is completely how\N除了吉姆提到的所有因素之外，还有什么变化？这些确实是技术细节，\N但真正改变的是我们看待机器人技术的整个方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.34,0:11:13.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,we approach robotics robotics so far has been the field of controls Controls was driving robotics until I would say even 3 4 years ago.\N以往机器人技术一直属于控制领域，控制理论主导了机器人技术的发展，直到大约三到四年前。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.20,0:11:18.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right now for those who have been in this area for a long time, they would know controls was not designed for robotics.\N现在，对于长期从事这一领域的人来说，他们知道控制理论原本并不是为机器人设计的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.32,0:11:25.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh like control had its really uh limelight during World War II for like flying planes, missiles and everything.\N比如说，控制理论在二战期间曾大放异彩，主要用于飞行器、导弹等的控制。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.39,0:11:29.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you had the craze for robotics began because of because of touring.\N然后，由于巡游的兴起，机器人热潮也随之而来。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.49,0:11:30.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then people like what do we use?\N然后人们开始思考，我们该用什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.00,0:11:33.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, let's use controls which were bu which was built for that.\N好吧，我们就用那些为这个目的而设计的控制装置吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.70,0:11:37.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that stuck around that stuck around for decades for 70 years.\N这种方式一直延续了数十年，长达70年。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.51,0:11:39.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it's not in the same spirit.\N但它的精神已不再相同。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.51,0:11:40.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not childlike learning.\N它不再是孩童般的学习方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.77,0:11:47.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,In child, you are not teaching them calculus first to learn how to walk like figure out your joint movements and then learn walk.\N在孩童身上，你不会先教他们微积分，再让他们学会走路，比如先弄清楚关节运动，再学习行走。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.70,0:11:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You are learning by experience.\N他们是通过亲身经历来学习的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.52,0:11:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So learning by experience is the main change that has happened.\N因此，通过经验学习是发生的最主要变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.44,0:11:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we are seeing all the sh all the shift happening.\N现在我们正看到所有这些转变正在发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.27,0:11:59.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I mean BD just released a video today learning by experience.\N嗯，我意思是，波士顿动力今天刚发布了一段视频，展示通过经验学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.66,0:12:02.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that is the I would say one major change has happened.\N所以，我认为这就是一个主要的变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.15,0:12:09.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Instead of programming experience from that we have gone to learning by experience which is a major shift how we think about robotics.\N与其依赖编程经验，我们转向了通过经验学习，这标志着我们思考机器人技术方式的重大转变。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.49,0:12:11.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to actually double click on that.\N我想实际上双击那个选项。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.94,0:12:18.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think for me right and I also been been in the field for long enough to be in the classical controls for\N我认为对我来说，而且我在这个领域也待了足够久，所以对经典控制方法也相当熟悉。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.27,0:12:27.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,team but um a large part of what happened was the internet right if you think about it like it's it's this enormous human experiment\N但其中很大一部分原因在于互联网，如果你这么想的话，\N这就像一场持续了近30年、全球各地的人共同参与的巨型人类实验。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.13,0:12:35.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,of like 30 close to 30 years of everyone around the world contributing to creating this enormous source of data so we can train an\N世界各地的人们共同贡献，形成了一个庞大的数据源，让我们得以训练人工智能，这简直是奇迹。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.49,0:12:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI which is completely magical and now what we're going to do is we're just going to ask all of you to do the same\N现在我们要做的，就是请在座各位在未来30年里也做同样的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.28,0:12:48.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,again the next 30 years just go around and be robots and no we're not going to do that but we had that data and\N再次重复，去四处走动，成为机器人，但其实我们不会这么做，不过我们已经拥有了这些数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.88,0:12:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,therefore that is what actually moved AI forwards even though it started in robotics and to me now what it's all about is how do\N正是这些数据真正推动了人工智能的发展，尽管它最初起源于机器人领域，而如今对我来说，\N关键在于如何利用现有数据，让机器人具备实际用途。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.32,0:13:06.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,we use that data that exists to bootstrap to where your robot can do something useful because at that point you can start to learn\N因为一旦机器人具备一定实用性，我们就能真正开始在现实世界中学习，而真正的智能正是源于现实世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.51,0:13:13.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the real world where where intelligence really comes from right but you have to get to where it is to a certain extent useful.\N但你必须先让机器人达到某种程度的实用性。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.52,0:13:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when I say go grab me a Coke in the fridge, if the robot's able to do so half the time,\N所以当我让机器人去冰箱里拿瓶可乐时，如果它能成功一半时间，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.28,0:13:22.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,then we have a feasible path to getting there because now we just need to say,\N那我们就已经找到了一条可行的路径，因为现在我们只需要说，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.34,0:13:29.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,okay, that worked, that didn't work, and we need to run it enough times and it'll get really good at getting me a coke in the fridge.\N好的，这个方法有效，那个方法无效，只要运行足够多次，它就能非常熟练地帮我从冰箱里拿可乐。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.23,0:13:35.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that is what we're seeing now with the advent of all of these multimodal LLMs is that you you can't\N我认为现在随着这些多模态大语言模型的出现，我们正看到这一点，即你无法
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.92,0:13:43.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,really solve robotics or intelligence in general I even think uh through this approach but you can get to where your system is\N真正通过这种方法解决机器人或一般智能问题，但你可以让系统变得
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.44,0:13:52.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,useful enough that you can create a very efficient data flywheel at scale that doesn't require you to teleoperate the robots for everything\N足够有用，从而在大规模上建立一个高效的闭环数据飞轮，而无需为每件事都远程操控机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.24,0:14:02.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,it does and that is probably the path to if not AGI at least based very very useful machines and maybe also to AI.\N这正是通往智能的路径，至少是极其有用的机器，也许还能通往人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.92,0:14:04.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll see down the road.\N我们以后会看到。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.31,0:14:07.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I feel like we got to circle back to to the last part you just said there.\N我觉得我们得回到你刚才说的最后一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.40,0:14:10.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in the meantime, Pros, I'm curious to hear your take.\N但与此同时，普罗斯，我很想听听你的看法。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.15,0:14:12.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think echoing some of Aaron's comments here.\N是的，我同意亚伦刚才的一些观点。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.80,0:14:16.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, why robotics is is kind of like coming back in.\N你知道，为什么机器人技术正在重新兴起。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.08,0:14:21.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, AI started with robotics and then kind of progressed to all these other areas and then sort of circled back.\N你知道，人工智能最初起源于机器人，然后逐渐发展到其他领域，现在又回来了。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.74,0:14:23.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, robotics is challenging for two reasons.\N好吧，机器人技术之所以具有挑战性，有两个原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.76,0:14:27.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,One, hardware is hard and the world is unstructured, right?\N首先，硬件很难，而世界是无结构的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.39,0:14:33.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you look at how AI has evolved, right, and how robotics has evolved,\N如果你看看人工智能是如何演进的，以及机器人技术是如何演进的，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.07,0:14:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,a huge portion of robotics has been dealing with the hardware is hard problem and miniaturizing sensors like MEMS,\N机器人技术的很大一部分都在应对“硬件很难”这一问题，并实现传感器的微型化，比如MEMS，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.60,0:14:43.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,building out actuator and drive technology, energy, energy storage technology.\N开发执行器和驱动技术，以及能源和储能技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.20,0:14:44.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of that stuff had to be solved.\N所有这些都必须被解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.78,0:14:51.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Even platforms like Arduino democratized people's ability to just get things to move in the real world\N即使像Arduino这样的平台，也实现了让普通人能够轻松让现实世界中的物体动起来，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.34,0:14:56.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,at all and and bring that to people so they weren't reinventing the wheel every single time.\N并将这种能力普及给大众，使他们不必每次都从头开始造轮子。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.14,0:15:05.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the AI side, we've been basically blocking our way through going from solving structured to increasingly unstructured problems.\N在人工智能方面，我们基本上是逐步突破，从解决结构化问题，转向越来越无结构的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.90,0:15:16.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Solving problems of queries and prompts to APIs to simplified world models to now unstructured world models.\N从解决查询和提示，到API，再到简化世界模型，如今是无结构世界模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.34,0:15:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh where every piece of this puzzle has been sort of upleveling the AI platforms, finding new ways to ingest data,\N每一块拼图都在不断升级AI平台，探索新的数据摄入方式，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.94,0:15:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,taking the best practices of the previous sort of structure and how that worked and then taking it to this next step of okay,\N借鉴之前结构化方法的最佳实践，并将其推进到下一步：那么，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.52,0:15:37.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,what if we remove some of these training wheels and now you're just looking at video coming from\N如果我们去掉一些训练用的辅助工具，现在你只是在看来自视频的输入
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.58,0:15:43.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,a self-driving car or now you're just looking at egocentric video being captured by a robot's uh cameras.\N一辆自动驾驶汽车，或者你现在看到的是机器人摄像头捕捉到的以自我为中心的视频。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.68,0:15:45.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,and what is going to happen next in this world.\N以及在这个世界中接下来会发生什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.02,0:15:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think there's a bit more of this progression at Unlock that's been happening behind the scenes and we're just seeing the culmination of\N所以我认为在 Unlock 上，这种进展在幕后已经持续了一段时间，我们现在才看到其最终的成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.32,0:16:00.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,that finally reach this tipping point where now okay we can go after this full problem of just interacting with the world in unstructured ways.\N这终于达到了一个临界点，现在我们可以着手解决与世界以非结构化方式互动的完整问题了。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.02,0:16:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the last thing you say there is so important though and talking about\N但我认为你刚才说的最后一点非常重要，特别是谈到
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.08,0:16:07.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,what has happened in hardware and maybe one of the biggest things happening the last few\N硬件方面发生的变化，也许过去几年中最大的变化是
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.03,0:16:13.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,years is the robustness of hardware and the ability to make hardware that doesn't break\N硬件的稳健性，以及制造出在与现实世界交互时不会损坏的硬件的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.21,0:16:16.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,when it interacts with the real world because all of us have worked long in robotics,\N因为我们所有人都长期从事机器人领域的工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.98,0:16:17.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.32,0:16:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Experiments take quite a long time when you need to rebuild the robot every time you run it.\N每次运行实验都需要重新搭建机器人，这使得实验耗时很长。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.28,0:16:25.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we're also now really at the point in hardware where we can have something learn\N但现在我们正处于硬件发展的关键阶段，可以让设备
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.58,0:16:29.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the real world and safely interact with the world without damaging itself or the world.\N在真实世界中学习，并安全地与世界互动，而不会损坏自身或环境。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.85,0:16:33.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's also a necessary condition really for this to progress.\N而且，这实际上也是这一进程得以推进的必要条件。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.27,0:16:34.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that took a long time.\N这花了很长时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.32,0:16:37.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's it's a pretty hard problem.\N这确实是一个相当困难的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.44,0:16:44.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, even listening to you all and and your your thoughts around this, it it brings up an interesting question.\N你们大家的讨论和想法让我想到了一个有趣的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.39,0:16:49.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think you all have very exciting and unique strategies and approaches.\N我认为你们所有人有着非常令人兴奋且独特的策略和方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.73,0:16:57.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I'm really curious to to hear your take on on your strategies and approaches for things such as the role\N我非常好奇想听听你们对这些策略和方法的看法，比如人工智能从专用模型向通用模型的转变。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.15,0:17:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,of AI uh moving from specialist to generalist models or how you think through things such as the explosion of foundation models.\N或者你们如何看待基础模型的爆发式增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.32,0:17:11.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I I can perhaps talk a bit about group's strategy, right?\N嗯，我可以简单谈谈我们团队的策略，好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.89,0:17:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're solving a really really hard problem uh to build a general purpose brain uh for for all kinds of different human robots not just one.\N我们正在解决一个极其困难的问题，即为各种不同的人形机器人构建一个通用的脑。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.84,0:17:22.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We also hope to get what we call cross embodiment.\N我们也希望实现所谓的跨具身。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.35,0:17:24.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So how do we tackle this problem?\N那么我们该如何应对这个问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.31,0:17:27.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would say uh there are two main principles.\N我认为主要有两个原则。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.27,0:17:33.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh principle number one is that the model itself we want it to be as simple as possible.\N原则一就是模型本身要尽可能简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.24,0:17:35.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want it to be as end to end as possible.\N我们希望它尽可能端到端。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.95,0:17:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh to the point that it's basically photons to actions, right?\N简直就是从光子直接到动作，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.80,0:17:48.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you take pixels in from like a video camera and then you directly output continuous floatingoint numbers which are essentially the control values\N你从摄像头输入像素数据，然后直接输出连续的浮点数，这些数值本质上就是电机的控制值。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.06,0:17:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,on the motor and that is the model end to end there is no intermediate steps as simple as possible and why is this\N这就是端到端的模型，中间没有中间步骤，尽可能简单，为什么这很好呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.52,0:18:02.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,good uh because if we look at the field of NLP and by the way NLP is a extremely perhaps the most successful field\N因为如果我们看看自然语言处理领域，顺便说一下，\N自然语言处理是目前被人工智能解决得最成功、或许也是最成功的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.03,0:18:11.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,so far uh that's being solved by AI and I think as roboticists we should copy homework copy homework from someone that already worked.\N所以作为机器人学家，我们应该向已经取得成果的人学习，照搬他们的方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.15,0:18:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for CHBT, right?\N就像 CHBT 一样，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.40,0:18:16.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Before CHBT, uh the field of NOP is kind of a mess, right?\N在 CHBT 之前，自然语言处理领域简直一团糟，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.66,0:18:19.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have text summarization, machine translation,\N你有文本摘要、机器翻译，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.77,0:18:28.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,code generation that's using completely different data pipeline and training protocols and model architectures, sometimes not just one model.\N代码生成，这些任务使用完全不同的数据流水线、训练协议和模型架构，有时甚至不是单一模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.56,0:18:34.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then Chad Gibbd came and just blew everything out of the waters because it's simple, right?\N然后查德·吉布斯出现了，一下子把一切都彻底改变了，因为它的方法非常简单，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.95,0:18:38.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It maps any text to any other text and that's it.\N它能将任意文本映射到任意其他文本，仅此而已。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.64,0:18:43.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,underneath is a transformer that maps a sequence of integers to another sequence of integers.\N其底层是一个将整数序列映射到另一整数序列的变换器。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.83,0:18:49.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And because it's so simple, you can unify all of the data, all of the problems into one model.\N正因为如此简单，你就可以将所有数据、所有问题统一到一个模型中。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.89,0:18:55.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that's where robotics should copy homework from to make the model as simple as possible.\N我认为机器人领域应该向作业学习，让模型尽可能简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.61,0:19:01.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the second principle is the data pipeline will actually be very complicated.\N第二个原则是，数据管道实际上会非常复杂。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.91,0:19:05.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like all the things that surround the model will be very complicated.\N就像围绕模型的所有东西都会非常复杂。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.39,0:19:10.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that is because for robotics as I said at the beginning data is a huge problem.\N这是因为正如我开头所说，机器人领域的数据是个大问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.64,0:19:14.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,You cannot download motor control data from YouTube from Wikipedia.\N你无法从 YouTube 或维基百科下载电机控制数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.97,0:19:16.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't find it anywhere.\N你根本找不到它。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.96,0:19:21.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh for GR00T our data strategy can be organized into a pyramid.\N所以对于 GR00T，我们的数据策略可以组织成一个金字塔。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.85,0:19:26.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right now close your eyes visualize a pyramid right at the top you have\N现在闭上眼睛，想象一个金字塔，顶部是
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.68,0:19:30.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,real robot data that's going to be highest quality because there is no domain gap.\N真实机器人数据，这将是最高质量的，因为不存在领域差距。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.80,0:19:31.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.08,0:19:34.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,You collect it using tally operation in the real world.\N你在现实世界中使用计数操作来收集它。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.15,0:19:43.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But that's got to be quite limited, not very scalable because we're limited by the fundamental physics limit of 24 hours per robot per day.\N但这样限制很大，扩展性很差，因为我们受限于每天每台机器人24小时的根本物理极限。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.40,0:19:43.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.95,0:19:44.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's it.\N就这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.81,0:19:47.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's really hard to scale in the world of atoms.\N在原子世界里实现规模化真的非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.36,0:19:49.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in the middle of the pyramid,\N在金字塔的中间位置，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.90,0:19:58.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's where simulation comes in where we rely heavily on physics engines like ISACH for example uh to to scale lots\N这就是仿真发挥作用的地方，我们大量依赖像 Isaac 这样的物理引擎来实现大规模扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.83,0:20:05.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,and lots of data and this data can be generated based on the real world collected data or through learning from\N以及大量数据，这些数据可以基于真实世界采集的数据生成，或通过学习获得。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.64,0:20:12.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,experience as as deep mentioned right so that would be simulation data and and just remember before NVIDIA was an AI\N正如之前深入提到的，那将是仿真数据，记住在英伟达成为AI公司之前
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.22,0:20:20.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,company it was a graphics company uh and what are graphics engines great for physics right rendering So that's our simulation strategy.\N公司最初是一家图形公司，而图形引擎在物理仿真和渲染方面非常出色，这就是我们的仿真策略。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.69,0:20:26.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And on the bottom of the pyramid, right, we still need all of those multimodal data from the internet,\N而在金字塔的底部，我们仍然需要来自互联网的所有多模态数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.67,0:20:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,but this time we use it a little bit differently, right?\N但这一次我们用它的方式稍微有点不同，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.08,0:20:35.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use it to train visual language models that can become the foundation for vision language action models.\N我们用它来训练视觉语言模型，这些模型可以成为视觉语言动作模型的基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.46,0:20:41.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the VMs are trained from lots and lots of internet, text, images, audio, you name it.\N这些视觉模型是从海量的互联网文本、图像、音频等数据中训练出来的，你想到的任何内容都有。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.62,0:20:50.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then recently there's also video generation models that become so good that they can be neuro simulations of the world.\N最近还出现了视频生成模型，它们变得如此出色，以至于能够成为世界的神经模拟。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.52,0:20:57.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the last layer of the pyramid is really the neuro simulation right that goes beyond traditional graphics engines.\N因此，金字塔的最顶层实际上是神经模拟，它超越了传统的图形引擎。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.51,0:21:02.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And these neuro simulations you can prompt a video generation model and ask for\N你可以向视频生成模型提出提示，要求它生成
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.92,0:21:08.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,things like you know hallucinate a new trajectory a new robot trajectory for me.\N比如说，想象一条新的轨迹，一条新的机器人运动轨迹给我。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.18,0:21:13.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the video models learn physics so well because it's trained on hundreds of millions of videos online.\N视频模型之所以能如此精准地学习物理规律，是因为它在数亿个在线视频上进行了训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.62,0:21:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it it trains it learns physics so well that it's able to give you physically accurate uh trajectories in\N它学习物理规律如此到位，以至于能够以像素形式提供物理上准确的轨迹。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.16,0:21:29.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,pixels and then you can run algorithms which we propose in group N1 something called latent action to extract back those\N然后你可以运行我们团队N1提出的算法，一种称为潜在动作的方法，从中提取出
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.44,0:21:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,actions from the hallucinated what we call the dreams of the robot right like the human robots dream of electric sheep\N那些从幻觉中生成的、我们称之为机器人“梦境”的动作，就像人类机器人梦中的电子羊一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.88,0:21:43.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,right it's it's dreaming and you collect those latent actions from it and you put it back into this data pyramid.\N是的，它在做梦，你从中收集这些潜在动作，并将其重新放入这个数据金字塔中。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.97,0:21:49.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with all of these very complicated data strategies, we compress them.\N在所有这些复杂的数据策略之下，我们会对它们进行压缩。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.21,0:21:54.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,We compress them into this one clean artifact from folds to actions, right?\N我们将它们压缩成一个清晰的单一成果，从折叠到动作，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.66,0:21:58.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,A two billion model suffices for a wide range of tasks.\N一个二十亿参数的模型就足以应对各种任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.25,0:22:00.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's an overview of Google strategy.\N所以这就是谷歌策略的概览。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.89,0:22:05.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think that paints a really kind of great future picture, right?\N我觉得这描绘出了一幅非常美好的未来图景，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.24,0:22:07.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have a simple big model.\N所以我们有一个简单的大模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.17,0:22:08.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's not even that big.\N呃，它甚至不算特别大。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.61,0:22:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that kind of solves everything pixels to motion, right?\N呃，它几乎能解决所有问题，从像素到运动，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.76,0:22:17.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think along the way we also need to pay attention to um all the things\N但我觉得在过程中，我们也需要关注所有这些
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.13,0:22:21.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,that that that we have to own delivering products out into the real world that require determinism.\N必须自己掌控才能将产品交付到现实世界中，且需要确定性的那些方面。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.83,0:22:22.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.16,0:22:29.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you uh need to deliver something to a customer, uh you need to understand what it's going to do in in unexpected conditions.\N所以当你需要向客户交付某样东西时，你必须理解它在意外情况下的表现。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.57,0:22:31.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to think about functional safety.\N你需要考虑功能安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.06,0:22:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,You need to think about um how it's going to regress if you uh add new capabilities uh um on top of existing ones.\N你需要思考一下，当你在现有能力基础上增加新功能时，系统可能会出现怎样的退化。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.16,0:22:43.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think you pointed out a really important thing which is the complexity gets pushed into the data right and the data that you gather.\N所以我认为你指出了一个非常重要的问题，即复杂性被推到了数据层面，也就是你所收集的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.83,0:22:47.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think we're at the very beginning of the journey of building that data set.\N我认为我们才刚刚开始构建数据集的旅程。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.12,0:22:54.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think you know maybe I would say uh a piece of uh uh strategy that we think is important is to make sure that you don't\N所以我想说，也许我们可以认为，一个重要的战略是确保你不会
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.99,0:22:59.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,throw the whole toolbox out in pursuit of this this potentially very powerful end state\N为了追求这个潜在的强大最终状态，而把整个工具箱都扔掉。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.65,0:23:02.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we have a lot of things to do as a community along the way.\N因为我们在这个过程中还有很多事情要做。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.27,0:23:06.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of them is to maintain the trust of the of the customers that are buying robots.\N其中之一就是维护购买机器人的客户对我们的信任。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.65,0:23:10.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh we have to be able to do that um by applying all of the tools we have.\N我们必须能够通过运用我们现有的所有工具来做到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.61,0:23:16.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think there's a lot of exciting uh new capabilities, things that we think will will totally change the landscape of robotics.\N我认为有很多令人兴奋的新能力，我们相信它们将彻底改变机器人领域的格局。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.68,0:23:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,They already are.\N它们已经做到了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.48,0:23:24.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,But at the same time, we need to also be realistic that there's a big toolbox of robotics tools going back 70 years.\N但与此同时，我们也必须保持现实，因为机器人领域已有长达70年的丰富工具积累。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.26,0:23:29.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And some of those are also the right tool to apply to solving real world problems.\N而其中一些工具也正是解决现实世界问题的正确选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.07,0:23:33.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh especially when you're doing things with large powerful robots that could hurt somebody or doing\N尤其当你在操作大型强大机器人时，它们可能会伤到人，或者在靠近人的环境中操作时，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.92,0:23:37.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,things around a person where you want to maintain that trust because as soon as you break\N你必须维持这种信任，因为一旦打破，就再也无法恢复了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.91,0:23:46.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,it you never get it back right so I think maybe I I just say there is a big toolbox that we need to apply yeah and I mean uh I second you very\N所以我认为，也许我刚才说的，我们确实需要一个庞大的工具箱来应对，是的，我非常赞同你，吉姆。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.30,0:23:50.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,much Jim and like we and we're very much in that camp where we're making like one\N我们也完全属于这个阵营，我们正在打造一个简单的模型，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.62,0:23:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,simple model we don't know exactly how it's going to look yet so I wouldn't call it\N目前还不确定它具体会是什么样子，所以我不会称它为非常简单，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.76,0:23:58.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,so simple but uh relatively simple model and it's all about the data right And if we\N但可以说是一个相对简单的模型，关键在于数据，对吧？如果我们
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.98,0:24:04.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,want to take the lessons learned from early LLMs and late LLMs in that in that case,\N想从早期大语言模型和后期大语言模型中吸取经验教训，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.27,0:24:10.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think one of the things that often gets underestimated is the importance of diversity.\N我认为有一件事经常被低估，那就是多样性的重要性。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.95,0:24:18.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So in the beginning of like this history of LLM, right, there's a lot of companies who tried to train, let's say, a very good model to create poems.\N比如在大语言模型的历史初期，有很多公司试图训练一个非常优秀的模型来创作诗歌。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.94,0:24:25.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they would train on all of the best poems in the world and it doesn't really work because unless you train on this\N他们用世界上所有最好的诗歌进行训练，但这并不奏效，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.58,0:24:33.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,very diverse data that has nothing to do with writing poems then you're not going to get intelligence because intelligence comes from that diversity.\N除非你训练的数据非常多样化，且与写诗毫无关系，否则你无法获得真正的智能，因为智能正是源于这种多样性。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.70,0:24:39.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we're seeing now at least in our models is that this is obviously also true for robotics.\N而我们现在在模型中看到的是，机器人领域显然也存在这种情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.97,0:24:44.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And even at the very small scale we are now in the beginning with these tiny data sets,\N即使在非常小的规模下，我们目前才刚刚开始使用这些小型数据集，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.07,0:24:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're actually more limited by diversity than we are by the scale of data.\N我们实际上受到数据多样性限制的程度，比数据规模的限制更大。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.28,0:24:55.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's about like how do you get as many tasks as possible in as many different environments as possible preferably\N所以关键在于如何在尽可能多的不同环境中，完成尽可能多的任务，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.51,0:25:02.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,with some much noise and dynamic stuff going on as possible so that like you can understand what an actual task is.\N尽可能多地引入噪声和动态变化，以便真正理解一个任务的本质。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.96,0:25:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh my favorite example is opening a washing machine.\N我最喜欢的例子就是打开洗衣机。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.16,0:25:11.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when we come in like and we see a washing machine, we see like okay, we're going to put the clothes into the round hole there.\N当我们看到洗衣机时，会立刻意识到，要把衣服放进那个圆形的入口里。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.57,0:25:17.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're going to try to open it and we try to find a handle and if it doesn't open, maybe there's a latch somewhere.\N所以我们会尝试打开它，寻找把手，如果打不开，可能某个地方有卡扣。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.85,0:25:20.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,If not, maybe we turn the dial back to zero.\N如果还是不行，也许我们把旋钮转回零位。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.38,0:25:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we have this great understanding of like how does the washing machine actually ex work, right?\N但我们对洗衣机实际工作原理有非常深刻的理解，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.52,0:25:27.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can figure out how to use a new one.\N所以我们能很快学会如何使用一台全新的洗衣机。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.62,0:25:29.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And machines today don't have that at all.\N但现在的机器完全不具备这种能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.70,0:25:32.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're kind of like learning how to repeat a motion.\N你有点像是在学习如何重复一个动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.85,0:25:42.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is why we really think the thing is so important about getting the robots out there in volume and really getting that diverse data.\N这正是我们之所以认为，让机器人大规模普及并获取多样化数据如此重要的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.53,0:25:47.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I guess here's our very contrarian view which I think is very interesting\N我想在这里提出一个非常反主流的观点，我认为这非常有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.05,0:25:50.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,to discuss because um that's why we mean like this has to happen among people.\N因为这就是我们的意思——这件事必须发生在人与人之间。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.02,0:25:57.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has to happen in the home and safety has to be an intrinsic thing to the machine, right?\N它必须发生在家庭环境中，安全必须是机器与生俱来的特性，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.16,0:26:02.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,How you ensure that the energy in the machine is not so big that it's dangerous.\N你如何确保机器的能量不会大到构成危险？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.68,0:26:12.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then thinking about how can we combine this with the classical toolboxes and uh yeah I think one thing I would like to\N然后我们再思考一下，如何将这一点与传统工具箱结合，嗯，我认为有一点我想补充的是，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.33,0:26:23.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,add here um is unlike LLMs or or vision when you say in uh robotics what's the approach it's always two things what's the approach\N与大语言模型或视觉不同，在机器人领域，当你说“方法是什么”时，\N总是有两个问题：硬件的方法是什么，软件的方法是什么，但没人问过语言领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.39,0:26:26.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,for hardware what's the approach for software nobody asked that for language\N为什么GPU的方法是什么，因为这部分已经由黄仁勋讲过了。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.90,0:26:30.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,what's the approach for GPUs because we have covered that covered by Jensen\N所以这就像，这里有两件不同的事，而这正是一个关键问题：是否应该只有一种机器人？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.26,0:26:37.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,so it is like but in There are two different things right and this is a major question like should there be only one robot\N是否应该只有一种 X 机器人，是否应该只有一种下一代机器人？我们究竟要部署哪种机器人？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.57,0:26:42.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,like should there be one x robot should there be one next robot like which robot are we deploying and then if you're deploying all\N然后如果你要部署所有机器人的话
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.50,0:26:48.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robots then is the brain shared across them and this is where I think the insight there are two things here one is humans\N机器人本身是共享大脑，而我认为这里的洞察在于有两个关键点，一个是人类
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.73,0:26:56.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,like anyone can come up from the audience and you can give them a VR suit like a tracking suit or some gloves or VR\N任何人都可以从观众席站起来，你可以给他们一套VR装备，比如追踪服或手套，或者VR头显
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.55,0:27:03.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,headset they can control any robot any robot and they don't need to know the motor details They don't need to know how the motors work.\N他们就能操控任何机器人，任何机器人，而且他们不需要了解电机的细节，也不需要知道电机是如何工作的
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.82,0:27:08.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It this is already an evidence that a brain can exist that can control any robot.\N这已经证明了一个大脑可以存在并操控任何机器人
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.38,0:27:09.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's the first aspect.\N这就是第一个方面
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.56,0:27:11.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can use data from anywhere.\N所以你可以使用任何地方的数据
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.21,0:27:14.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the second thing is there is no data out there.\N现在第二个问题是，根本没有数据存在
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.26,0:27:15.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody knows that, right?\N大家都知道这一点，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.84,0:27:23.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we are missing one special robot that is out there and we have tons of that data and that those robots are humans.\N但我们缺少一种特殊的机器人，而这种机器人恰恰存在，我们拥有海量关于它们的数据，这些机器人就是人类
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.27,0:27:24.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are not mechanical robots.\N我们不是机械机器人
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.03,0:27:27.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are not designed by electricity.\N我们不是由电能驱动的
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.20,0:27:28.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are biological robots.\N我们是生物机器人
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.80,0:27:35.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,But at the end of the day similar principles guide us like you have motor neurons like they are called motor neurons sensory neurons.\N但归根结底，类似的原理指导着我们，比如你有运动神经元，它们被称为运动神经元，还有感觉神经元。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.08,0:27:40.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sensory neurons carry signal from your sensors to your brain and motor neurons from brain to your motors.\N感觉神经元将信号从你的传感器传送到大脑，而运动神经元则将信号从大脑传送到你的执行器。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.59,0:27:45.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if we are agreeing that a brain can exist that controls all hardware.\N所以如果我们同意，大脑可以存在并控制所有硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.02,0:27:48.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why should we exclude the biological hardware?\N那为什么我们要排除生物硬件呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.54,0:27:54.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you don't exclude that you can actually use human video data of human human activity.\N如果你不排除它，实际上就可以使用人类活动的视频数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.66,0:28:00.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we may not have a 1X robot let's say doing something picking up opening a fridge but humans\N比如我们可能没有1X机器人，比如说正在捡起或打开冰箱，但人类
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.36,0:28:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,open fridge every other like 10 times a day there are trillions of videos out there of humans doing it.\N每天大约十次左右就会打开冰箱，网上有数以万亿计的这类人类操作的视频。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.28,0:28:14.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is uh at least our belief is that this is one of a very critical data for robotics like how human limbs operate how this so you can actually\N所以我们认为，这至少是机器人领域非常关键的数据之一，比如人类肢体是如何运作的，这样你就可以
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.44,0:28:18.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,use that knowledge to uh to go towards in addition to simulation of course it's not\N利用这些知识，当然还要结合仿真，但如果没有这些数据，仿真并不完整，因为你不能仅仅只是观看和播放。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.39,0:28:21.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,complete without that because you cannot just watch and and and play uh so but these\N但这些因素可以结合起来，我认为这非常迅速，我认为
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.94,0:28:27.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,things can combine together I think this is oh so very quickly I think this I\N我们非常一致，我的意思是，所有这些数据都极其有用，我们
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.59,0:28:31.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,think we very much agree I mean all of that data is incredibly useful and we\N也完全同意。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.79,0:28:35.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,use it too like this is these are not usually that data is needed I just\N也用它，就像这些数据通常并不需要，我只是
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.81,0:28:38.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,want try to clarify the point that this point was getting mixed in two things here.\N想试着澄清一下，这个观点在这里被混淆了，涉及两个不同的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.90,0:28:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, it's good.\N不，这样很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.60,0:28:42.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I I can tell pro has some strong thoughts on this too.\N而且我能看出来，Pro 对这个问题也有很强烈的看法。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.89,0:28:51.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, as someone who's teleyoperated a lot of robots, I can I can say that sure the human brain is great at telly operating a variety of platforms,\N作为一名经常进行远程操作机器人的人，我可以告诉你，当然人类大脑在远程操控多种平台方面确实很出色，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.14,0:28:55.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I can tell you from experience, not at the same level of performance.\N但根据我的经验，性能并不能达到同一水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.41,0:28:58.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,The hardware can definitely make a difference.\N硬件确实会产生影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.49,0:29:03.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and and definitely I mean I I've teley operated a 1X robot, right?\N嗯，而且我确实远程操作过 1X 机器人，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.26,0:29:05.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's a great experience, right?\N那是一次很棒的体验，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.41,0:29:10.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,have teley operated some industrial robots not a great experience um the hardware\N我也远程操作过一些工业机器人，那体验并不好，硬件
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.96,0:29:14.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,can matter a lot in this and does define some of the characteristics of\N在这方面确实很重要，它决定了性能的一些特性，
Dialogue: 0,0:29:14.46,0:29:22.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,performance and I think that's important to note that there will be differences and there is some amount of building the right hardware to make it be\N我认为这一点很重要，那就是会存在差异，而且确实需要打造合适的硬件才能实现理想效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.47,0:29:30.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,controllable to have the right sensing to have the right inertial properties um to make it effective in the real world I mean we have Aaron here\N可控的，具备正确的感知能力，拥有合适的惯性特性，才能在现实世界中真正有效。我们这儿就有亚伦。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.37,0:29:36.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,who has like wowed the world with that for the last 10 years right that the dynamics of the machine matters and you can really see it.\N过去十年里，正是它让世界为之惊叹，机器的动态特性确实至关重要，你真的能看出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.73,0:29:44.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,it moves in a different one example is like we are missing here which is not here like Darwaini robot people use that robot for doing surgery like\N它在另一个不同的领域中，比如这里缺失的一个例子，就是达芬奇手术机器人，人们用它来进行手术。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.54,0:29:48.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh that's already a hundred billion plus company and all they do is teleoperation\N呃，那家公司市值已经超过一千亿美元，而他们做的只是遥操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.95,0:29:52.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,through uh through through this like this is amazing like so which means that nobody's\N通过啊，通过，就这样，太惊人了，也就是说，没人能
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.94,0:29:56.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,disagreeing on the fact that human brain is very powerful and hardware so these\N在人类大脑非常强大且硬件如此先进的这一事实上有分歧
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.96,0:30:01.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,questions are kind of that's why robotics is always these two things like approach\N问题本质上就是为什么机器人总是涉及这两个方面，比如方法论
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.07,0:30:08.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,can be different in the end they all have to come together so it's not like one hardware or the other like it's like uh but real world data,\N最终可能各不相同，但它们都必须融合在一起，不是单一硬件或另一硬件的问题，而是真实世界数据的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.27,0:30:11.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,human data, simulation and scaling from all these things.\N人类数据、仿真以及从所有这些事物中进行的扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.31,0:30:16.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's also a bit about like bottom up and tops down right because now we're talking very much top down on the control architecture.\N我认为这在某种程度上也关乎自下而上和自上而下的问题，因为现在我们讨论的控制架构非常侧重自上而下。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.87,0:30:21.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think it's also very interesting with the bottom up of like how do you learn dexterity for example, right?\N但我觉得从底层来看，比如如何学习灵巧性，这一点也非常有趣，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.90,0:30:29.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh at least we're experiencing that learning like inhand quick dexterity in teleop uh\N而且至少我们正在体验到这种在遥操作中快速灵巧的手部操作学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.13,0:30:32.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,we don't know how to do it like uh we don't know how to build\N我们不知道该怎么做，就像我们不知道如何构建
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.48,0:30:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,a teleoperation system to do so that's fast and good enough and really gives you\N一个能够快速且足够好地实现远程操作的系统，真正提供触觉反馈
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.76,0:30:39.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,tactile feedback and all these things but the robot can actually learn it really well.\N以及所有这些功能，但机器人实际上能学得很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.39,0:30:41.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you just give it a bunch of objects to play with,\N所以如果你只是给它一堆东西去玩，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.59,0:30:45.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is learnable and then it becomes a question of how do you kind of\N这是可学习的，然后问题就变成了你该如何
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.92,0:30:52.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,lift the interface in a uh like add an abstraction layer basically on your teleoperation interface.\N提升接口，基本上在远程操作接口上增加一个抽象层。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.09,0:30:54.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you're no longer saying like hey I'm going to pinch grasp like this.\N所以你不再说“我要这样夹住”。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.93,0:31:02.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're more like guiding the machine for like what tasks to be done and allowing the system to actually learn dexterity.\N你更像是在引导机器完成哪些任务，并让系统真正学会灵巧性。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.19,0:31:03.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh yeah, yeah,\N是的，没错，
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.71,0:31:07.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think there's there's one thing that that I think we tend to skip when we\N我认为当我们试图将大脑与硬件分离时，有一个点我们常常忽略，
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.30,0:31:11.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,try to separate the the brain from the hardware and that's the task you're trying to do.\N那就是你正在尝试完成的任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.02,0:31:15.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you're if you're thinking about a whole set of tasks where the objects are small,\N所以如果你在考虑一组任务，而物体都很小，
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.90,0:31:21.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're inertially irrelevant, um yeah, you can separate a lot of the brain from the body.\N它们在惯性上无关紧要，是的，你可以把大脑的很多部分从身体上分离出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.44,0:31:25.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think the reality is that mostly what we want to build these machines\N但我认为现实是，我们主要想制造这些机器
Dialogue: 0,0:31:25.15,0:31:29.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,for extends beyond the simple tabletop tasks that I think a lot of people start with.\N其应用范围已超越了大多数人最初接触的简单桌面任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.74,0:31:31.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you want to be lifting big,\N如果你想举起又大又重的物体，
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.49,0:31:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,heavy complex objects or you want to be touching sharp sheet metal parts or you\N或者接触锋利的金属板部件，又或者你
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.44,0:31:39.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,want to be working with something hot because you can remove a person from a\N想处理高温物体，因为你可以让人离开
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.81,0:31:44.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,manufacturing environment and take them away from the hazard and replace that with a robot\N制造环境，远离危险，用机器人替代
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.24,0:31:47.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,then I do think hardware really does matter and I think it has to co-evolve.\N我认为硬件确实很重要，而且必须同步演进。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.52,0:31:56.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the idea that we can kind of have a complete disconnection between you know a good hardware platform with an API and any software brain.\N我认为，我们完全可以将一个优秀的硬件平台与API，和任何软件大脑完全脱钩，这种想法是错误的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.72,0:32:04.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think sometimes you know those two things need to co-involve understanding the the kind of quality of your actuator how much\N有时候你知道，这两件事需要共同参与，理解你的执行器的特性以及它的性能水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.55,0:32:10.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh um friction it has in it uh can matter a lot for how well you can represent it in simulation for example.\N嗯，它内部的摩擦力在模拟中可能影响很大，比如在表示它时。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.00,0:32:17.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think uh we're going to need to have more time before I think we fully understand how a model like GR00T, for example,\N而且我认为，在我们完全理解像 GR00T 这样的模型之前，可能还需要更多时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.49,0:32:23.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,deploys on a robot that's of type A and a robot that's of type B because I don't think we have enough data points yet\N部署在类型A的机器人和类型B的机器人上，因为我认为我们目前的数据点还不够多
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.17,0:32:30.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,to say that one model will deploy across all of these different kinds of robots and there won't be significant differences in the resulting behavior.\N说一个模型能部署在所有这些不同类型的机器人上，并且不会导致行为出现显著差异
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.96,0:32:34.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if I'm trying to pick a bag of chips and move them and drop them, I don't think it matters.\N如果我只是想捡起一包薯片并移动它们再放下，我认为这并不重要
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.57,0:32:40.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if I'm trying to pick, you know, a high precision part and assemble it in another high precision hole, it might matter a lot.\N但如果我要捡起一个高精度零件，并将其装配到另一个高精度孔中，这可能就非常重要了
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.70,0:32:44.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think there the jury's out for me on whether you can really separate those two things.\N所以我认为在这方面，我还在观望，不确定是否真的能区分这两者
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.65,0:32:48.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it really depends on what I think what could be other way around too.\N而且这实际上还取决于我认为是否可能反过来也成立
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.60,0:32:50.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like one hardware has lots of brains.\N比如某种硬件拥有大量智能
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.51,0:32:50.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.80,0:32:54.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the NVIDIA one hardware lots of companies putting brains.\N就像英伟达的硬件，许多公司都在往上面添加智能
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.64,0:33:01.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I I think Aaron actually touched on a very interesting topic and a very difficult challenge of cross embodiment, right?\N所以我认为亚伦实际上触及了一个非常有趣且极具挑战性的话题，也就是跨具身问题，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.20,0:33:04.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what does cross embodiment mean uh for a model?\N那么对一个模型来说，跨具身到底意味着什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.27,0:33:07.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,So le let's maybe think a second about ourselves.\N所以让我们或许再花一秒钟思考一下我们自己
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.55,0:33:10.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think actually humans are great at cross embodiment.\N我认为人类实际上非常擅长跨具身。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.96,0:33:16.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like anytime you open up a video game and you start playing it, you're actually doing a cross embodiment, right?\N比如你打开一个视频游戏并开始玩的时候，实际上就是在进行跨具身，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.58,0:33:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you are uh let's say you know doing driving car in a game or\N比如你，呃，假设你在游戏里驾驶汽车或者
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.60,0:33:25.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,like playing some like weird character sometimes like non-human character and then after a while right\N玩一些奇怪的角色，有时甚至是非人类的角色，然后过一会儿，对吧
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.13,0:33:28.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,after you play with a joystick a little bit you'll get a feel of how you\N在用操纵杆玩了一小会儿之后，你就会逐渐感受到如何
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.64,0:33:33.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,control that body inside the virtual game and after a while you can play it super well.\N控制虚拟游戏中的那个身体，过一会儿你就能玩得非常好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.75,0:33:36.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So actually human the human brain is great at cross embodiment.\N所以实际上，人类的大脑非常擅长跨具身。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:36.94,0:33:38.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it I think it's a solvable problem.\N所以我认为这是一个可解决的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.02,0:33:42.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just need to find that set of parameters to enable this.\N我们只需要找到那组能实现这一能力的参数。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.48,0:33:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh I agree with Aaron that for now it's too early.\N而且我同意亚伦的观点，现在还为时过早。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.57,0:33:49.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's still it's still quite early to talk about like full zero shot\N目前还太早谈论完全的零样本
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.73,0:33:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,cross embodiment meaning that you bring a robot and the model just magically works.\N跨具身，意思是把一个机器人和模型放在一起，它就能神奇地直接工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.00,0:33:55.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I don't think so.\N嗯，我觉得不是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.28,0:33:55.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.71,0:33:57.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's we're not there yet.\N我们还没到那个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.33,0:34:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but someday we will and I think like one way to have that is to\N嗯，但总有一天我们会做到，我认为其中一种方式是
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.52,0:34:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,have lots and lots of different robot hardware and even more different robot hardware in simulation.\N拥有大量不同类型的机器人硬件，甚至在模拟中拥有更多不同的机器人硬件。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.64,0:34:16.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so previously our research group had a very interesting work but I would say still like a kind of toy you know exploratory work called metamorph.\N嗯，之前我们的研究小组做过一项非常有趣的工作，\N但我觉得仍然像是一种玩具，一种探索性的工作，叫做变形体。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.74,0:34:24.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what we did is in simulation we procedurally generated a lot of simple robots with like you know different kind of joint connectivity.\N我们在模拟中程序化生成了大量简单的机器人，具有不同的关节连接方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.80,0:34:28.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it can look like a snake, look like a spider, really weird.\N它们看起来像蛇，像蜘蛛，甚至非常奇怪。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.05,0:34:30.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we generate thousands of them.\N但我们生成了成千上万这样的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.82,0:34:37.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we use a robot grammar to tokenize to tokenize the body of the robot, right?\N然后我们使用机器人语法对机器人的身体进行分词，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.46,0:34:41.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Essentially converting the embodiment itself to a sequence of integers.\N本质上是将实体本身转换为一串整数。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.79,0:34:45.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And once we see a sequence of integers, right, then we see transformers.\N一旦我们看到一串整数，对吧，那么我们就能看到变换器。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.91,0:34:47.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Attention is all you need, right?\N注意力机制就是一切，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.61,0:34:48.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,We see transformers.\N我们看到了变换器。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.61,0:34:52.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,We apply transformers to this whole set of thousands of embodiment.\N我们将变换器应用到这数千种具身形态上。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:52.79,0:34:57.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we find that you can actually able to generalize to the thousand first embodiment.\N我们发现实际上可以泛化到前一千种具身形态。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.44,0:35:00.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,But again, it's a very toy experiment super early.\N但再次强调，这只是一个非常简单的早期实验。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.19,0:35:04.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I do believe that if we're able to have like a universal description language and\N但我相信，如果我们能够拥有一个通用的描述语言，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.39,0:35:08.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have lots of different types of real robot and simulation robot and we can tokenize them,\N并且拥有各种真实机器人和仿真机器人的类型，还能将它们分词化，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.03,0:35:13.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can generate lots of data from them, then all the embodiment become this kind of universe,\N我们就能从它们中生成大量数据，从而使所有具身形态变成这样一个宇宙，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.98,0:35:20.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,the space, vector space of embodiment and perhaps a new robot will be within distribution.\N具身形态的向量空间，也许新的机器人会落在这个分布范围内。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.21,0:35:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I also want to add that this is not just an intellectual curiosity.\N我还想补充一点，这不仅仅是一个智力上的好奇。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.40,0:35:25.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's becoming a very real problem.\N它正成为一个非常现实的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.02,0:35:26.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.67,0:35:32.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So um I I think all of the uh hardware company founders here have this issue where you have different\N嗯，我觉得在座的所有硬件公司创始人可能都面临这个问题，就是你们有不同的
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.34,0:35:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,generations of a robot and the data you collected on the previous generation and the model you train on that data.\N一个机器人的多代演化，以及你从上一代机器人收集的数据，和基于这些数据训练出的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.80,0:35:43.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,It doesn't generalize or it degrades significantly even to your own company's V2 and V3 robot.\N它无法泛化，甚至在你们公司自己的 V2 和 V3 机器人上性能也会显著下降。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.93,0:35:49.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,actually uh like even forget that within the same version of the robot because\N实际上，甚至不用考虑同一款机器人版本之间的差异，因为
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.89,0:35:54.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,of manufacturing because of all the little right defects it's a physical world it's messy\N由于存在各种微小的缺陷，制造过程是一个物理世界，充满混乱
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.16,0:35:59.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,right because of all the messiness uh different robots don't even always replicate the\N因为各种混乱，不同的机器人甚至无法完全复现。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.41,0:36:04.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,same model perfectly right you have cross embodiment issue even within one generation of the\N不同的机器人甚至无法完美复现同一个模型，即使在同一世代内也存在跨具身性问题
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.78,0:36:09.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,robot let alone across generations let alone across different company and designs so it's\N机器人，更不用说跨代际，更不用说跨不同公司和设计了，所以这很困难
Dialogue: 0,0:36:10.04,0:36:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,becoming a real problem and I think we're just scratching the surface yeah there's not\N已成为一个真正的问题，我认为我们才刚刚触及表面，是的，这还远未结束。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.68,0:36:16.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,a lot of diversity right now honestly and if you if you look in\N现在多样性确实很多，如果你仔细观察的话
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.37,0:36:20.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,the humanoid space it's it's we're all pretty much working with a fairly similar thing.\N人形机器人领域，我们其实都在使用相当相似的技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.88,0:36:22.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's an it's the replication of our body.\N这是对我们身体的复制。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.84,0:36:27.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um at at Bostonamics we decided to only use three fingers for our gripper\N在波士顿动力，我们决定只用三个手指来设计夹爪
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.12,0:36:31.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you know it was bucking the trend of having a fully anthropomorphic hand.\N而这实际上违背了追求完全类人手型的主流趋势
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.81,0:36:37.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and we found like, you know, humans are so good at mapping themselves even to three fingers, right?\N嗯，我们发现，人类其实非常擅长用三个手指进行自我映射，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.36,0:36:43.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you can have a teley operator operate a three-finger gripper and within a couple hours of training in the telly rig,\N所以，你可以让一名远程操作员在远程操作训练装置上训练几小时后
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.48,0:36:45.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're doing kind of everything you do with five fingers.\N就能完成原本需要五根手指才能做的事
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.85,0:36:48.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think there's a lot of space to explore here.\N所以我认为这里还有很大的探索空间
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.22,0:36:53.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I think because everybody's trying to get a foundation built right now, we're not being very brave.\N嗯，我觉得现在大家都在努力搭建基础，所以大家还不够勇敢
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.98,0:36:58.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think what's going to happen uh uh as soon as you see these generalizations start to\N但我想，一旦你看到这些泛化能力开始
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.95,0:37:02.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,show uh up in our models is you'll see you'll see people break away from these a little bit.\N在我们的模型中显现出来，人们就会开始逐渐摆脱这些传统设计
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.86,0:37:04.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that might be good or might be bad.\N这可能带来好处，也可能带来坏处
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.11,0:37:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think, you know, we may end up with robots that look uh just far enough away from humans that it's scary.\N我觉得，我们最终可能会造出一些机器人，外形离人类足够远，以至于让人感到害怕
Dialogue: 0,0:37:09.04,0:37:15.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,But uh I think just inside of the the manipulator alone, there's such a a rich space of opportunities there.\N但我觉得，仅在夹爪本身，就已经存在一个极其丰富的可能性空间
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.54,0:37:17.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think agility's got, you know,\N我认为 Agility 有一种，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.10,0:37:22.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,a completely different gripper than anything you see on on these other humanoids and they're still able to do some of these same tasks.\N一种与其它人形机器人上看到的完全不同的夹持器，但他们仍能完成一些相同任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:22.70,0:37:25.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think that's going to be an exciting topic uh in the coming years.\N所以，我认为这将在未来几年成为一个令人兴奋的话题。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.00,0:37:29.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, Aaron, you give me a thousand different Atlas, I'll solve it for you.\N是的，亚伦，你给我一千个不同的 Atlas，我都能帮你解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.52,0:37:30.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.46,0:37:31.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.41,0:37:31.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Deal.\N成交。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.92,0:37:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, I feel like you already answered my my next question, which was specifically around hardware.\N嗯，我觉得你已经回答了我下一个问题，就是关于硬件的具体问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:36.52,0:37:37.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, thank you all.\N谢谢大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.61,0:37:37.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.87,0:37:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I want to continue on that because it is a really interesting\N但我还想继续说下去，因为这非常有趣
Dialogue: 0,0:37:41.12,0:37:48.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,challenge that you all have such really insight into and and from unique perspectives.\N你们所有人都具备如此深刻的洞察力，并且拥有独特的视角，这是一大挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.40,0:37:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Would you say what what you were just talking about I mean even you Jim when\N你刚才说的，我是说，吉姆，你提到的同一个机器人，它制造出来后表现可能不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.12,0:37:57.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,you were mentioning more so about the same robot bot that's manufactured it might perform differently.\N这取决于具体情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.55,0:37:58.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,It just depends.\N这取决于具体情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.48,0:38:02.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is that would you say the biggest challenge right now when it comes to hardware?\N你认为目前硬件方面最大的挑战是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.63,0:38:05.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think that's definitely one of the one of the challenges.\N我认为这绝对是其中一个挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:05.75,0:38:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and that also prompted us to kind of study this line of research on cross embodiment on how we can bridge some of these gaps.\N呃，这也促使我们开始研究跨具身这一方向，探讨如何弥合这些差距。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.12,0:38:14.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but I will defer this question to all product experts here.\N呃，这个问题我将留给在场的所有产品专家来回答。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.85,0:38:19.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is back to where I think you'll find that this is where the the rest of the toolbox matters, right?\N这又回到了我认为的关键点：这时其他工具箱里的工具就显得很重要，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:19.91,0:38:28.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you make a robot that that um has really good calibration methods, if you make a robot that you understand how to characterize,\N所以如果你制造的机器人具备非常出色的校准方法，如果你清楚如何表征它，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.09,0:38:31.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you do a lot of the good work on the joint level control, right,\N如果你在关节层级控制上做了大量扎实的工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.17,0:38:35.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,the stuff that sits way below the AI, then I think some of these things aren't as big a deal.\N那些位于AI之下的基础工作，我认为这些问题就没那么严重了。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.59,0:38:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think when you have a robot that you can't characterize, that you haven't calibrated, uh,\N所以，当你面对一个无法表征、未经过校准的机器人时，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.00,0:38:45.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,that has a lot of variability from copy to copy and you just kind of throw a controller at it,\N这种情况在不同副本之间差异很大，你只能随便扔个控制器上去试试。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.68,0:38:50.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,whether it's an AI policy or whether it's something else, I think you find a lot of variability in the output.\N无论是AI政策还是其他什么，我认为输出结果的差异性都很大。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.04,0:38:53.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, but I think you can do a lot of work to minimize that gap right now.\N嗯，但我认为现在你可以做很多工作来缩小这种差距。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.02,0:38:56.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I I think you probably have some thoughts here as well.\N我想你在这里可能也有一些想法。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.30,0:38:58.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think uh another aspect to this is just, you know,\N是的，我认为这背后还有另一个方面，就是你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.96,0:39:04.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,getting robots out there in in the real world and and doing manufacturing and seeing what variability you have.\N让机器人真正进入现实世界，进行制造，观察实际的差异性。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.50,0:39:08.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,you do get a lot of learnings that do feed back into the pipeline you build.\N你会获得大量反馈，这些反馈会回流到你构建的流程中。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.41,0:39:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so a great example of this is, you know, Digit has a recovery behavior that's fully learned, right?\N嗯，一个很好的例子是，Digit具备完全通过学习获得的恢复行为，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:13.78,0:39:15.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've been deploying it out in the real world.\N我们已经在现实世界中部署了它。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.98,0:39:17.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's it's on our production systems.\N它已经运行在我们的生产系统上。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.89,0:39:18.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.10,0:39:24.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the domain randomization and and um diversity of data that we use to train that uh comes from it's fed back\N我们用来训练该模型的领域随机化和数据多样性，正是从这些实际部署中反馈回来的。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.78,0:39:31.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,from what we experienced in the real world and the variation in all of the digits that we've we've got in our fleet.\N来自我们在现实世界中的经验，以及我们车队中所有数字的多样性。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.18,0:39:37.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it turned out that uh we were doing so much of this domain randomization and and hardening the policy so\N嗯，结果发现，我们做了大量领域随机化，并强化了策略，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.14,0:39:44.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,much that when we transferred the policy to our new robot which we just debuted which is like 10 kg heavier.\N以至于当我们把该策略迁移到我们刚发布的新型机器人上时，它比之前重了约10公斤。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:44.17,0:39:46.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like a much larger frame.\N它的框架要大得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.15,0:39:53.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,The policy actually just one shot transferred to this totally new robot, slightly different kinematics, heavier payload, everything.\N该策略实际上一次就成功迁移到了这台全新的机器人上，\N尽管其运动学特性略有不同，负载更重，其他各方面也完全不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.47,0:39:53.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.70,0:40:01.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it's because we had been spending all of this time like hardening and uh robustifying like all of the\N这是因为我们花了大量时间来强化和提升策略的鲁棒性，\N真正理解了仿真到现实迁移过程中的所有细节，比如脚部接触等。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.01,0:40:08.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,sim tore transfer really understanding like all the details of things like foot contact and um all of these pieces.\N所以我认为，随着经验积累，你在跨具身迁移方面会变得越来越熟练，这并不仅仅意味着
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.62,0:40:14.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I do think that with experience you get better at this cross embodiment and it isn't just\N你总是需要极其仔细地查看机器人的制造序列号。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:14.43,0:40:19.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're always doomed to need to like look at the manufacturing serial number of the robot super carefully.\N随着你不断实践并积累现实世界的经验，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.20,0:40:23.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's some amount of as you do it and as you get experience with the real world,\N你会更清楚地理解在训练流程中需要捕捉哪些关键因素。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.04,0:40:29.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,you understand more about what the levers are that you need to capture in the training pipeline.\N你就能更深入地掌握训练流程中真正起作用的那些调控杠杆。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.38,0:40:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think you're confronted by when you get from when you go from hundreds to thousands of robots.\N我觉得当你从几百台机器人扩展到上千台机器人时，就会面临这样的挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.60,0:40:34.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not a choice.\N这不是一种选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.96,0:40:41.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't be tuning your your software stack per robot when you have thousands or hundreds of thousands of robots.\N当你拥有成千上万甚至数十万台机器人时，不可能为每台机器人单独调优软件栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.06,0:40:43.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think it's it's just something that has to happen.\N所以我认为，这注定会发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.76,0:40:48.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I kind of agree with both of you, but like I agree a lot here with like calibration matters.\N我某种程度上同意你们两位的观点，但在这里我特别认同校准的重要性。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.19,0:40:48.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It matters a lot.\N这非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.04,0:40:49.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.68,0:40:55.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but I think it's very interesting actually and uh maybe it's a bit too deep but\N嗯，但我觉得这实际上非常有趣，也许有点太深入了，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:55.04,0:41:00.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,like when you do domain randomization what you're actually teaching your system right is to be conservative.\N比如说做域随机化时，你实际上是在教系统保持保守。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.06,0:41:04.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're teaching your system to like oh if I don't know what will happen if I do this I'm safe anyway.\N你是在教系统：如果我不确定做这件事会有什么后果，那我就保持安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:04.61,0:41:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.02,0:41:07.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this kind of masks your dynamics.\N这种做法实际上掩盖了系统的动态特性。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.33,0:41:09.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it really depends on what you're trying to achieve.\N所以这实际上取决于你想要实现什么目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:09.80,0:41:13.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like you won't get the same performance out of the system if you domain randomize.\N比如说，如果你进行领域随机化，系统就无法获得相同的性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.54,0:41:15.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,But of course you will get something that's very robust.\N但当然，你会得到一个非常稳健的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.54,0:41:19.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you do really good calibration, you can kind of like get more out of your system.\N所以如果你进行非常精确的校准，就能从系统中获得更多的效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.14,0:41:20.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it will matter in the long term.\N从长远来看，这将变得非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.99,0:41:29.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then I think there's some incredibly exciting work going on right now with adding the robot history to the context of the model.\N我认为现在有一些非常令人兴奋的工作正在进行，就是将机器人历史信息加入模型的上下文中。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:29.22,0:41:32.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you for every single individual robot,\N所以对于每一个单独的机器人，
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.15,0:41:37.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,you take some of that robot's runtime and you put it into the history to the context of\N你提取一部分该机器人的运行时数据，并将其放入模型的实际上下文中，
Dialogue: 0,0:41:37.61,0:41:45.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,the actual model and then it learns kind of its own dynamics in context which actually works surprisingly well.\N这样模型就能在上下文中学习到自身的动态特性，这实际上效果出乎意料地好。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:45.50,0:41:53.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I mean we and this is this this is really cool and that's kind of like getting uh that's the work we it's called RMA rapid motor application.\N嗯，我们正在做这项工作，这真的很酷，这其实就是我们所说的 RMA——快速电机应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.47,0:42:00.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's this idea but I want to give a slightly different flavor to this uh uh this this thing that it's a big problem that you cannot\N这就是这个想法，但我想要给它一个稍微不同的角度，就是这个问题很严重，你无法在不同版本之间更改模型，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.79,0:42:08.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,change your model across versions like uh and it's very hard to expect that there will be only one robot one company all the robots in the world\N而且很难指望世界上只有一款机器人、只有一家公司生产所有机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.03,0:42:16.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's nowhere there like like in cars there are so many car companies in mobile phones so many mobile phone companies right so but the thing is for\N在汽车领域，有那么多汽车公司，而在手机领域，也有那么多手机公司，但问题是
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.99,0:42:20.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,them and even for like uh for every other application there's so many GPUs\N对他们来说，甚至对其他所有应用来说，都有这么多GPU
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.85,0:42:25.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,NVIDIA creates but then you have CUDA layer which abstracts you away from it.\N英伟达创造了这些，但你还有CUDA层，它让你远离了硬件细节
Dialogue: 0,0:42:25.24,0:42:32.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh right for this that's true for operating system what is the equivalent for robotics when it's come to solving uh robotics.\N嗯，对于操作系统来说，机器人领域对应的等价物是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.09,0:42:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So here I would say the slightly different t take here for every other field since we are always abstracted away from the hardware\N所以我认为，对于其他领域，这里需要一个稍微不同的视角，因为我们总是被硬件抽象所隔离
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.88,0:42:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,whether it's vision language like it does that like if a new company has to come in let's say AMD or any other company they\N无论是视觉还是语言，如果新公司要进入，比如AMD或其他公司，他们
Dialogue: 0,0:42:47.24,0:42:53.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,have to make sure that everybody else can seamlessly run their NVIDIA code or their their code that runs on NVIDIA GPUs on their\N必须确保其他人都能无缝运行他们的英伟达代码，或者在英伟达GPU上运行的代码，也能在他们的GPU上运行
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.85,0:43:03.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPUs it's their burden it's not not the software burden for the analogy for AI is the brain for the robot that we are building.\N这是他们的责任，而不是软件开发者的负担，类比来说，AI就像是我们正在构建的机器人的大脑
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.17,0:43:09.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We shouldn't be building the brain that just works on the robot but rather a brain that adapts on the robot.\N我们不应该只构建一个只在特定机器人上运行的大脑，而应该构建一个能适应机器人的大脑
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.92,0:43:17.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's the major difference like what humans have is not uh is not is not a system which can do many things.\N这就是关键区别，人类拥有的并不是一个能做很多事情的系统
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.46,0:43:19.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the system which can learn to do many things.\N而是一个能学会做很多事情的系统
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.78,0:43:24.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we are carrying in our head is a learning engine like it can learn on the fly.\N我们头脑中携带的，是一个能实时学习的引擎
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.59,0:43:32.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,like whatever you hear you are learning on the fly and adapting on the fly and that's what will be the major break like major difference\N就像你听到的任何信息，都是实时学习并实时适应的，这将是主要的突破，也是主要的区别
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.56,0:43:36.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,between how AI has been done for everything else and for robotics like\N在人工智能应用于其他领域和应用于机器人技术之间的区别在于
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.56,0:43:41.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,for robotics what we will be deploying really are these mini learning engines uh\N对于机器人技术，我们将部署的实际上是这些微型学习引擎
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.53,0:43:49.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,and they are because many things happen like for instance forget about other humans and other other cars etc even basic thing your own body if\N因为会发生很多事情，比如，别提其他人类或其他车辆了，就连你自己的身体也一样
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.74,0:43:57.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,I go to do workout one after 1 hour workout my hands are sore uh and I have to pick up a toothbrush or even a bottle,\N我做完一小时的锻炼后，手会酸痛，连牙刷甚至瓶子都拿不起来
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.15,0:44:05.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have a different body now because my body now requires lot more torque to get the same output than it did before workout.\N我的身体现在不同了，因为锻炼后，要达到同样的输出，身体需要更多的扭矩
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.11,0:44:11.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So our brain is adapting on the fly to these changes happening in every microsconds to minutes to uh long hours.\N所以我们的大脑正在实时适应每秒、每分钟乃至数小时内的这些变化
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.69,0:44:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is what the the main difference uh I believe should be or will be when\N这正是我认为主要的区别所在，或者说是未来
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.76,0:44:21.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,these AI models get on the robot compared to how they have been applied to anywhere else.\N当这些人工智能模型被部署到机器人上时，与它们在其他地方的应用方式相比
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.64,0:44:30.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,like anywhere else the study has been simple train deploy train deploy you don't have to worry about adaptation no changing because NVIDIA is taking\N在其他地方，研究模式很简单：训练、部署、再训练、再部署，无需担心适应问题，因为不会变化
Dialogue: 0,0:44:30.16,0:44:36.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,care of you as the GPUs get better you are taken care of any company comes in you are taken care of but in robotics that\N因为英伟达会照顾你，随着GPU性能提升，你始终被照顾着，任何公司进入，你都依然被照顾
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.32,0:44:43.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,will be the difference you will be deploying learning engines which is why this is a much very different application of AI than anything that we\N但在机器人领域，这将是根本区别，你将部署的是学习引擎，因此这与我们以往任何AI应用都完全不同
Dialogue: 0,0:44:43.44,0:44:53.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,have seen so far but I think in general this distinction between like robotics AI and other digital AI I also think that will go away.\N到目前为止，但我认为总体上，机器人AI与其他数字AI之间的区别也会消失。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:53.14,0:44:53.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:44:53.80,0:45:01.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think we ask the question what can AI do for robotics way too much these days and we don't ask the question\N所以我认为我们最近一直在问AI能为机器人做什么，但很少问
Dialogue: 0,0:45:01.28,0:45:08.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,what can AI sorry what can robotics do for AI because the data that you get when you're actually taking actions in the real\N机器人能为AI做什么，因为当你在现实世界中真正采取行动时，你会获得数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.17,0:45:16.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,world and you have a hypothesis you take an action you observe the result and you're learning that's how we learn right and we\N你提出一个假设，采取行动，观察结果，然后学习，这就是我们学习的方式，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.72,0:45:24.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,we see a lot of things in reasoning models lately for example being incredibly good at math being incredibly good that code because it's verifiable.\N最近我们看到很多推理模型在某些方面表现得非常出色，比如数学和代码，因为这些结果是可以验证的。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.50,0:45:27.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can go and see like did I get it right?\N你可以去检查一下，我做对了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.53,0:45:30.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, robots kind of allow you to do that for everything.\N而机器人则让你能对所有事情都做到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:30.70,0:45:32.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's how we learn.\N这就是我们学习的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:32.64,0:45:34.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in that sense, I think I completely agree.\N从这个意义上说，我完全同意。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.96,0:45:36.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Another example is hallucination.\N另一个例子是幻觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.64,0:45:38.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hallucination is a big problem in LLMs.\N幻觉是大型语言模型的一个大问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.04,0:45:41.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have you ever heard robots hallucinating?\N你听说过机器人产生幻觉吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:41.04,0:45:42.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like this is not a discussed topic we discuss.\N就像这不是一个我们讨论过的话题。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.91,0:45:43.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why?\N为什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:43.11,0:45:44.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because robots cannot hallucinate.\N因为机器人无法产生幻觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:44.36,0:45:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because if I have to hallucinate, what will happen if I push this bottle from here to here?\N因为如果我必须产生幻觉，那当我从这里推这个瓶子到那里时会发生什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.84,0:45:48.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can just try it.\N我可以直接试试。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:48.62,0:45:49.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will drop.\N它会掉下来。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.19,0:45:49.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can see.\N我能看见。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.81,0:45:51.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't have to.\N我没必要。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:51.05,0:45:52.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I learn by interaction.\N我通过互动来学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:52.83,0:45:58.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,So since I interact, interaction is the enemy of hallucination because as you interact, hallucination goes away.\N所以因为我是在互动，互动就是幻觉的敌人，因为随着你不断互动，幻觉就会消失。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.39,0:46:02.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,While when you're learning from passive data where data is coming from Wikipedia,\N而当你从被动数据中学习时，数据来自维基百科，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:02.59,0:46:09.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can't go and verify everything unless it's math or coding where hallucination is less of a problem because you can actually verify the answer.\N除非是数学或编程这类幻觉问题较少的情况，否则你无法验证所有内容，因为你可以实际验证答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:09.19,0:46:09.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:09.46,0:46:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what happens is we get way more data.\N所以我们能获得多得多的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.20,0:46:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like you said, we flip the pyramid.\N就像你说的，我们颠倒了数据金字塔。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.56,0:46:13.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isn't that what Yuki says?\N那不正是由纪说的吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:13.53,0:46:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We flipped the pyramid and now we get this um robot data being way bigger than the internet and\N我们颠倒了数据金字塔，现在机器人数据的规模远超互联网。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.64,0:46:23.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can solve a lot of the problems we have today and all we need is a lot more GPUs.\N我们能解决今天面临的许多问题，而我们所需要的只是更多GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.57,0:46:26.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we absolutely that's always the answer.\N我认为这绝对是答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:26.95,0:46:29.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's why we're all here, right?\N对，这正是我们所有人在这里的原因，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.22,0:46:31.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think you absolutely can have hallucination, right?\N我觉得你当然可能产生幻觉，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.91,0:46:37.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it manifests in a different way which is a deviation in the robot's expected outcome from what happens in the real world.\N它以另一种方式表现出来，即机器人预期结果与现实中的情况出现偏差。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.82,0:46:43.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now it's verifiable in the same way that like code generation hallucinations are verifiable when they don't compile, right?\N现在它和代码生成中的幻觉一样可验证，比如代码无法编译时，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.78,0:46:45.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it it manifests in, you know,\N但它会表现为，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.60,0:46:51.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,a robot doing a trajectory that's infeasible or or generating out of what I mean is it can go away since you can interact.\N一个机器人执行了不可行的轨迹，或者生成了脱离实际的内容，也就是说，\N因为它可以互动，所以问题可以被解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.59,0:46:56.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, if you do not have the ability to interact, you it can never go away like uh for instance,\N但如果你没有互动能力，这个问题就永远无法解决，比如，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:56.76,0:47:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can never know like uh like if you cannot I don't know like do you live at this location?\N你永远无法确定，比如，你是否住在这个位置？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:02.44,0:47:05.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,If I cannot verify, I can never correct my hallucination.\N如果我无法验证，我就永远无法纠正我的幻觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:05.35,0:47:08.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in in robotics you can mostly correct because of interaction.\N但在机器人领域，由于可以互动，我们通常能进行修正。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.49,0:47:15.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have a very good practical example actually because we did this uh it was actually last year u where we had the problem of no\N其实我有一个非常实际的例子，因为我们去年就遇到过这个问题，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.32,0:47:22.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,one putting down the toilet seat in the office and we had one of our previous robots the eve uh some wheels but it's still very mobile.\N办公室里没人会把马桶盖放下来，我们当时用了一台之前的机器人，它有轮子，但仍然非常灵活。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:22.77,0:47:29.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we had it autonomously go in and see if the toilet seat is up or down.\N所以我们让它自主进入，检查马桶盖是打开还是关闭。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:29.36,0:47:32.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we ran uh GPT40 on this, right?\N我们在这上面运行了 GPT-40，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.96,0:47:35.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it was 50% up or down.\N结果是50%的概率是打开或关闭。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.23,0:47:36.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it had no idea.\N完全不知道状况。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:36.17,0:47:37.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was random, right?\N随机的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:37.19,0:47:39.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,It couldn't tell if the seat was up or down.\N它分不清座椅是升起来还是降下去了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:39.71,0:47:43.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's kind of an edge case because it's usually pretty good at these things.\N嗯，这算是个边缘情况，因为通常它在这些事情上表现得还不错。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:43.14,0:47:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we had the robot go and close the toilet seat.\N但我们让机器人去把马桶盖关上了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:45.52,0:47:46.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an autonomous policy.\N这是一个自主策略。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.01,0:47:51.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it would go around and like check the bathroom and put the toilet seat down if the toilet seat was up.\N所以它会绕着走，检查一下卫生间，如果发现马桶盖是掀起来的，就会把它放下来。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.56,0:47:57.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that was really fun and we had a lot of fun and we laughed about it and but it's actually closing the loop in the real world, right?\N这真的很有趣，我们玩得很开心，也为此笑过，但其实这在现实世界中真正实现了闭环，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:57.75,0:48:00.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now the model can get the feedback of seat is down.\N现在模型能获取到座椅已放下的反馈了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.75,0:48:02.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know the seat is down.\N我知道座椅已经放下了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.38,0:48:03.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I closed it.\N我关了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.28,0:48:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know it's down.\N我知道它已经放下了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.33,0:48:05.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you told me it was up.\N而你告诉我它原来是掀起来的。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:05.93,0:48:06.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You were wrong.\N你错了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.88,0:48:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's similar to closing the loop in in other places where we're using AI to interact with, for example,\N这类似于在其他使用人工智能进行交互的场景中闭合回路，例如，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:12.56,0:48:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,APIs or compilers or things like that where you you have it emit some result and then\N与 API 或编译器或类似工具交互时，你让系统输出某个结果，然后
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.04,0:48:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,you put it through a verification phase that you can feed back into the context of the system.\N将其放入验证阶段，再将结果反馈回系统的上下文中。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.60,0:48:24.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just in this case the loop closure is a little bit slower because it's going through the Yeah,\N只是这种情况下，回路闭合的速度稍慢一些，因为它要经过，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.93,0:48:29.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,the problem right now is that we don't know how to do this. uh in a general case, right?\N目前的问题是，我们还不知道如何在一般情况下做到这一点，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:29.06,0:48:34.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can we can architect one specific thing like the toilet seat and now the question is how do you come up\N我们可以为某个特定事物设计架构，比如马桶座，但现在的问题是，如何
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.72,0:48:40.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,with some formulation of this problem where you're grounding everything in the real world and no one knows how to do that yet.\N建立这个问题的通用表述，使所有内容都基于现实世界，而目前还没有人知道该怎么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.72,0:48:44.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,The rate at learning in the real world is going to be painfully slow, right?\N在现实世界中的学习速度将会非常缓慢，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.38,0:48:49.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can learn these things in the real world because there are consequences to dropping something.\N所以我们只能在现实世界中学习这些，因为丢东西会有后果。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.12,0:48:50.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Gravity makes it fall.\N重力会让它下落。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.14,0:48:52.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can tell something bad happened, right?\N你能看出发生了不好的事情，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.06,0:48:54.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the rate at which we can explore with a physical robot.\N但使用物理机器人进行探索的速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:54.91,0:48:57.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean that's back to the the blend of data, right?\N我的意思是，这又回到了数据的融合，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.83,0:49:06.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean you can do these really exciting small things but how many thousands or millions of those things do you need to do before you have enough data?\N我的意思是，你可以做这些非常令人兴奋的小规模事情，但在拥有足够数据之前，\N你需要完成成千上万甚至数百万次这样的操作？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.12,0:49:12.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think the the the question is really uh still can we afford to produce the real world data?\N所以我认为，真正的问题仍然是，我们是否负担得起生成真实世界数据的成本？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.49,0:49:13.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have simulation too.\N你还有仿真。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.84,0:49:16.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So simulation is also also also interactable.\N所以仿真也是可交互的。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.23,0:49:18.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think it's interaction data you can have both.\N所以我认为，你既可以拥有交互数据，也能获得仿真数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.01,0:49:19.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I agree.\N我同意。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.38,0:49:22.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And simulation also needs more GPUs.\N仿真同样需要更多的 GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.80,0:49:30.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, I know we're we're getting close to time and I really wanted to uh end with this question because I'm very curious about this.\N好的，我知道我们快到时间了，但我真的很想以这个问题结束，因为我对此非常好奇。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.96,0:49:35.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the next two to five years, where do you see this headed?\N在接下来的两到五年里，你认为这会走向何方？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.07,0:49:37.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm going to leave that as a vague vague question.\N我就把它作为一个模糊的问题留给大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.75,0:49:39.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Answer it how you will.\N你怎么回答都行。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.06,0:49:40.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'd love for you to start, Burnt.\N我想让你先开始，布恩特。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.54,0:49:40.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.79,0:49:45.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, two to five years, that's a big pretty big range given the current velocity of the field.\N所以，两到五年，考虑到当前领域的进展速度，这个范围相当大。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.36,0:49:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, but but let me like say I'm going to cheat and I'm going to say start by saying I think it's going to take 10 years before this fully pans out.\N但让我坦白说，我打算作弊一下，我想说，我认为要让这一切完全实现，需要十年时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.68,0:49:57.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and it's very easy to say where will this be in 10 years.\N嗯，说十年后会是什么样子，这很容易。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:58.00,0:50:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think then we're going to have the same kind of change in society that we had few hundred years\N我认为，我们将会经历一场与几百年前电力普及时类似的社会变革。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.44,0:50:06.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,ago with electricity where we now just take it for granted when you flip the light switch in the morning.\N那时我们已经习以为常，早上一开灯就亮了。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.40,0:50:13.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's going to happen to labor across digital and physical and man is it an interesting thing time to be alive and I think\N这种变化将发生在数字和物理劳动领域，而人类正处于一个非常有趣的时代，\N我认为这正是我们能真正聚焦于人性本质的时候。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:13.21,0:50:21.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can really get to focus on what makes us human uh in in that society we're creating five years I hope we're there\N我希望五年后我们能达到那个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:21.31,0:50:28.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's ambitious we're going to push for it uh I don't think anyone knows at this point uh I think it really\N我觉得这很有雄心，我们会为之努力，但目前没人真正知道，\N我认为关键在于社会接纳机器人有多快，以及我们制造规模扩大的速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:28.63,0:50:38.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,depends on how fast society adopts robots and how fast we can scale manufacture We're at kind of like the cusp where it's useful,\N我们正处于一个关键节点，此时机器人变得真正有用。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.96,0:50:39.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.44,0:50:44.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I would say the product we have just as an example is currently useful in a home.\N所以，以我们目前的产品为例，它在家庭环境中已经很有用。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.57,0:50:45.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not perfect.\N它并不完美。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.53,0:50:48.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not like you don't need to do anything yourself,\N并不是说你完全不需要自己动手，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.30,0:50:55.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it's useful and it's fun and then you can kind of start accelerating from there and\N但它确实有用，也有趣，然后你可以从这里开始逐步加速，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.88,0:51:02.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh hopefully it's not an autonomous car and uh doesn't take a decade longer than we think.\N希望它不是一辆自动驾驶汽车，也不会比我们预期晚十年才出现。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.22,0:51:11.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I do think like uh three to five years it is pretty much out there amongst most people and even if not everyone\N但我认为，三到五年内，它基本上已经普及到大多数人身边，即使不是每个人都拥有机器人，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.04,0:51:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,has a robot people know someone who has a robot and they're generally part of society uh across everything from consumers and homes into factories,\N人们也认识有机器人的人，它们普遍存在于社会各个层面，从家庭消费者到工厂、物流等各个领域，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:21.08,0:51:24.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,logistics, everything else.\N无所不在。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:24.40,0:51:25.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I can go next.\N好的，我来下一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.94,0:51:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh so there's a saying that people often uh overestimate the the progress in the short term but they often underestimate the\N有一句常说的话，人们往往高估短期内的进步，却常常低估长期的进步。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:34.84,0:51:40.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,progress in the long run and I think this is probably by Bill Gates or someone u and uh so I cannot\N我觉得这句话大概出自比尔·盖茨或类似的人，但我记不清了。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.84,0:51:50.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,again this is a disclaimer but I think the one thing unique about robotics AI that makes it different from LLMs or\N再次强调，这只是一个免责声明，但我认为机器人 AI 有一个独特之处，使其不同于大型语言模型或
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.34,0:52:00.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,VLMs is that LLM LLM has to really solve the problem almost to the completion to be really useful like uh whether it's\N视觉语言模型：大语言模型必须几乎完全解决问题，才能真正有用，比如无论是
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.14,0:52:06.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,coding whether it's uh general uh writing or anything it has to be really really good like NLP had good systems earlier\N编程，无论是通用写作还是其他任务，都必须非常出色，就像早期自然语言处理系统那样优秀。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.44,0:52:13.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,but until you reach like really high in performance these are not useful but that's not quite true for robotics AI because uh\N但除非性能达到非常高的水平，否则这些并不实用，不过机器人AI的情况并非完全如此，因为嗯
Dialogue: 0,0:52:13.16,0:52:19.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,we don't have to solve robotics fully for robotics to be useful and this is just a just to say like even\N我们不必完全解决机器人技术，机器人就已经能发挥作用了，这只是想说明一下，即便如此
Dialogue: 0,0:52:19.44,0:52:26.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,today there are like hundreds of thousand to millions of robots deployed already out Many of our things are made by robots today,\N如今已有数十万到上百万台机器人被部署使用，我们日常的许多产品如今都是由机器人制造的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.98,0:52:27.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.39,0:52:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they are already out there.\N所以它们已经在那里了。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.60,0:52:29.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're already there.\N他们已经在那儿了。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:29.38,0:52:30.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what is the key part here?\N那么这里的关键是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:30.84,0:52:35.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,The key thing in robotics is that this there is decision of tasks.\N机器人技术的关键在于任务的决策。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:35.33,0:52:38.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,The robot that solves all task everywhere that may be farther.\N能够解决任何任务、在任何地方应用的机器人，可能还很遥远。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:38.99,0:52:40.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I'll not make any prediction for that.\N所以我不会对这一点做出任何预测。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.82,0:52:46.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we will start seeing robots that make that maybe solve few task or one task or two task or task specialist.\N但我们将开始看到能够解决少数任务、单一任务或两个任务，或是特定任务的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.87,0:52:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And even they are super useful uh because there are several tasks for which it's very difficult to either find labor or hire.\N即使它们非常有用，因为有些任务很难找到或雇佣到劳动力。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.68,0:52:59.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was talking to some uh company today that they they are unretiring people from retirement because this is a shortage of labor for for\N我今天和一家公司交谈时提到，他们正在让退休人员重返工作岗位，因为这正是劳动力短缺的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:59.78,0:53:08.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,their specific uses for specialized robots will much come much quicker and uh generalist one will be farther but the usefulness starts from day one in\N针对特定用途的机器人将很快出现，而通用型机器人则会更远一些，但实用性从第一天起就已显现。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.19,0:53:16.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,robotics unlike uh unlike language that's so true and if autonomous cars weren't dangerous the problem was solved in 2015 you could get into a car\N机器人领域的情况与语言完全不同，这一点非常真实，如果自动驾驶汽车不危险，\N问题早在2015年就解决了，你那时就能坐上一辆自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.87,0:53:24.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,that drove you around in 2015 and it was doing pretty well solved from uh uh in one way as in it's not human way solved.\N那辆车在2015年已经运行得相当不错，从某种意义上说问题已解决，只是并非以人类的方式解决。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:24.45,0:53:25.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yeah.\N嗯，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.15,0:53:25.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.62,0:53:30.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's part of the challenge is that um adoption is is not just a technological problem.\N我认为挑战的一部分在于，采用不仅仅是一个技术问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:30.31,0:53:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's it's also, you know, things like safety, things like um societal uh adoption also play a factor.\N它还涉及安全等问题，以及社会层面的接受度，这些因素同样重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.28,0:53:38.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so in in 3 to 5 years,\N所以在三到五年内，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:38.81,0:53:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,what we might see is that there's a lot more robots in certain areas and a lot fewer robots in certain areas than we expected.\N我们可能会看到，某些区域的机器人比预期多得多，而另一些区域则少得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:45.57,0:53:52.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and I think the the important thing though is we are really seeing the culmination of robots really going\N而且我认为重要的是，我们正真正看到机器人技术的集大成时刻，它们终于开始真正落地了。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:52.84,0:54:01.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,from being historically very single purpose to this notion that it's almost expected that they could be multi-purpose maybe not\N从历史上非常单一用途，转变为如今这种几乎预期它们具备多用途的观念，也许并非完全如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:01.20,0:54:09.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,general purpose but multi-purpose that's becoming kind of people's expectation and the the what we're able to show with these\N也许不是通用，而是多功能，这正逐渐成为人们的一种期待，而我们通过这些展示出的能力正是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.38,0:54:15.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,new AI based platforms is that hey a a piece of hardware can can do more than one thing effectively.\N新的基于人工智能的平台的妙处在于，一块硬件能够高效地完成多种任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.36,0:54:19.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that's the piece that will hold over the next 3 to 5 years\N我认为这才是未来三到五年里能持续保持的关键所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:19.26,0:54:24.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,is this expectation as the new waterline that people are are building towards and you know all\N这是否已成为人们新的努力方向，就像新的基准线一样，你们知道的
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.13,0:54:27.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,of you are now seeing this and buying into it which is great right because now\N你们现在看到并认同这一点，这很棒，因为现在
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.66,0:54:32.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're you're going to be sort of carrying that expectation socioulturally forward and and saying like you\N你将在社会文化层面持续承载这种期待，不断强调这一点
Dialogue: 0,0:54:32.92,0:54:37.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,know hey why can't I have a robot that does three or four things in a\N知道吗，为什么我不能有个能做三到四件事的机器人呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.25,0:54:41.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,home or in my case you know five or 10 things in a warehouse or logistics facility\N在家，或者像我这种情况，在仓库或物流设施里，五到十样东西
Dialogue: 0,0:54:42.02,0:54:46.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,like that should that should be how it is and I think that's what really drives it\N就像那样，就应该这样，我认为这才是真正的驱动力。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:46.53,0:54:53.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,is is people wanting those things really drives uh investment and focus into getting us those things.\N真正想要这些事物的人，才是推动投资和聚焦，让我们获得这些事物的关键。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.84,0:54:54.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.03,0:54:59.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,When people ask this question, they're looking really concrete specific like I'm going to have a robot at this date, right?\N当人们问这个问题时，他们往往非常具体，比如我将在某个日期拥有一个机器人，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:00.04,0:55:01.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's going to do all these things.\N它将完成所有这些任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:01.63,0:55:07.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think the the real problem with this is there's no level setting on what expectations are for everybody, right?\N我认为真正的问题在于，大家对预期没有统一的标准，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:07.41,0:55:14.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the the question I usually ask is, you know, when will we have a humanoid robot that's as valuable to us as our car?\N所以我通常会问：我们什么时候才能拥有一个像汽车一样对我们有价值的机器人？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.36,0:55:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have no idea, right?\N我完全不知道，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.16,0:55:20.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our car works every day in the most extreme weathers.\N我们的汽车每天都能在最极端的天气下正常运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:20.48,0:55:24.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it costs hardly anything given the amount of material and effort that goes into putting into it.\N考虑到投入的材料和努力，它的成本几乎可以忽略不计。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.02,0:55:31.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and even the car by itself isn't quite uh touching what a humanoid robot might add to the value of our lives.\N即使是汽车本身，也还远未达到人形机器人可能为我们的生活带来的价值水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.86,0:55:35.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think, you know, I'm I'm also in the like 10 years or longer.\N所以我认为，嗯，我也是认为至少需要十年或更久。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:35.19,0:55:37.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that's the typical like technologist answer.\N而这正是技术人士典型的回答。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.63,0:55:39.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,If I if you ask a founder, they're going to say next year.\N如果你问一位创始人，他们会说明年。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.65,0:55:42.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you ask a technologist, they're going to say it's about 10 years, right?\N如果你问一位技术专家，他们会说大概还有十年，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.86,0:55:47.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And 10 years just means it's really hard for us to quantify specifically what you're going to have.\N而十年意味着我们很难具体量化你将来会拥有什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:47.59,0:55:52.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the thing we should be focusing on is the rate of progress and where the beach heads are, right?\N我认为我们应该关注的是进展速度以及各个切入点在哪里，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.37,0:55:57.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of the the the groups up here is establishing a meaningful beach head in a different area.\N这里每个团队都在不同领域建立了有意义的切入点。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.26,0:55:59.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over time, those things are going to grow.\N随着时间推移，这些都会不断成长。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.22,0:56:01.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that space is going to go from a bunch of dots, right?\N那个领域将从一堆零散的点，变成什么样子，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:01.93,0:56:05.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,where, you know, agility solving problems in a warehouse.\N比如说，敏捷机器人在仓库里解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.09,0:56:07.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have robots in uh in people's homes.\N我们已经有机器人进入人们家中。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:08.00,0:56:10.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, we're going to be working on automotive factories.\N嗯，我们还将着手汽车工厂的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:10.93,0:56:14.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think you're going to see from each one of these beach heads, you're going to see a growth, right?\N我认为你会看到，从每一个切入点出发，都会出现增长，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:14.35,0:56:16.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's not going to be an over in the night thing.\N而这不会是一夜之间就发生的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.60,0:56:21.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't think anybody here can predict 5 years into the future and say exactly where we're going to be,\N我认为这里没有人能预测五年后的情况，也无法准确说出我们将会在哪里，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.20,0:56:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I think we're going to see this this growth.\N但我认为我们会看到这种增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:22.90,0:56:27.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And pretty soon all those things are going to start overlapping and one day we're going to have an autonomous car.\N而很快，所有这些技术都将开始重叠，总有一天我们会拥有自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.27,0:56:31.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you look back at that history of that market, you know,\N当你回顾这个市场的历史时，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.10,0:56:37.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,there was a lot of uh um shade thrown out on how badly they predicted, you know, when we would have an autonomous car.\N当时有很多人批评他们预测得多么糟糕，比如我们什么时候才能拥有自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.31,0:56:43.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think a lot of that came from statements that that some elements in the community were making on how quickly it would come.\N我认为这其中很大一部分原因，来自社区中一些人关于技术实现速度的过于乐观的言论。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:43.29,0:56:47.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I'm pretty grateful that my car does autonomous lane assist and, you know,\N但我很感激我的车具备自动驾驶车道保持功能，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:47.99,0:56:52.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,doesn't hit the car in front of me and and and and prevents me from backing into something.\N它不会撞上我前面的车，也不会让我倒车时撞到东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.33,0:56:56.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,All that magical stuff came out of the dream of having an autonomous car.\N所有这些神奇的功能，都源于对自动驾驶汽车的梦想。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.30,0:56:58.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And oh, by the way, you can get in an autonomous taxi right now.\N顺便说一句，你现在就可以乘坐自动驾驶出租车。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:59.04,0:57:00.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, yeah, it took a little longer.\N所以，是的，它花的时间稍微长了一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.91,0:57:02.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and and so will humanoid robots.\N人形机器人也是一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.68,0:57:08.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think as long as the community is is excited, leans in, and and and realizes this is a long game, right,\N我认为只要社区保持热情，积极投入，并意识到这是一场长期战役，就对了，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.91,0:57:15.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,to get to specialist robots that are delivering value in a commercial setting, I think we we're going to have that in the next one or two years.\N要实现能在商业场景中创造价值的专业机器人，我认为我们将在未来一到两年内实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.43,0:57:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, agility is already delivering robots into into this space.\N事实上，敏捷公司已经将机器人投入这一领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:19.12,0:57:24.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we get those robots doing 10, 15, 20 tasks, that's going to be in that next 5 year terrain.\N当这些机器人能够完成10、15、20项任务时，那将进入未来五年的发展阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.49,0:57:29.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,But when we're going to solve all of the problems we imagine across all of the industries,\N但要解决我们想象中横跨所有行业的所有问题，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.09,0:57:32.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,um I think we need to keep dreaming and we keep working and and this industry is going to\N我认为我们需要持续梦想，持续努力，这个行业还需要投入大量精力，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.88,0:57:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,have to keep putting energy in for many more decades I think until we've solved all those edge cases.\N我觉得需要持续投入几十年，直到我们解决所有边缘情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.36,0:57:44.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I really like uh Deepuk saying that you know people tend to overestimate the short term and underestimate the long term.\N我真的很喜欢迪帕克说的那句话：人们往往高估短期进展，却低估长期潜力。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:44.80,0:57:47.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let me break it down into short-term and long term.\N那么让我把问题拆解为短期和长期两部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:47.70,0:57:55.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the next two to five years uh from a technical perspective we will be able to study fully the embodied scaling law.\N我认为从技术角度看，未来两到五年内，我们将能够全面研究具身缩放定律。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.90,0:58:05.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think the biggest moments in large language models is uh the original chinchilla scaling law uh basically that exponential curve where you put in\N我认为大型语言模型最大的突破在于最初的奇努卡缩放定律，本质上就是那条指数曲线：\N你投入更多算力，就扩大数据量，扩大参数数量，智能就会呈指数级上升。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.06,0:58:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,more compute you scale the uh amount of data you scale the number of parameters and you will just see intelligence just going up right exponentially.\N你投入更多算力，就扩大数据量，扩大参数数量，智能就会呈指数级上升。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.60,0:58:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh I don't think we have anything like that for robotics yet because the scaling\N嗯，我认为目前我们还没有类似的东西用于机器人领域，因为规模扩展还处于早期阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.60,0:58:23.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,law is so complicated for robotics right you can scale across model you can scale across\N机器人领域的缩放定律实在太复杂了，你可以扩展模型，也可以扩展
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.15,0:58:27.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,the hardware fleet right the real robot data and how about the simulation data scaling\N硬件集群、真实的机器人数据，以及仿真数据的扩展性如何？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:27.21,0:58:32.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,law how about the internet data scaling law how about the neural simulation the neuro uh\N那互联网数据的缩放定律呢？神经模拟呢？神经……
Dialogue: 0,0:58:32.46,0:58:36.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,dreams right scaling law as you are generating lots and lots of videos so we\N神经梦境，对吧？当你生成大量视频时，缩放定律
Dialogue: 0,0:58:36.68,0:58:41.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,will be able to study all of these things so that perhaps you know five years\N将能够研究所有这些内容，或许五年后你就会知道
Dialogue: 0,0:58:41.50,0:58:50.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,from now or sooner from Then we'll have that plot uh on the screen that you know exactly how many GPUs you buy and how much better your robot will be.\N从现在起，或者更早，我们就能在屏幕上看到这个图表，\N清楚地知道你购买多少块GPU，你的机器人就会变得多好。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:50.94,0:58:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we'll answer that question quantitatively very soon in the short run.\N因此，我们很快就会在短期内定量回答这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.96,0:58:58.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now uh let's talk about what's going to happen in 20 years.\N现在呢，我们来谈谈二十年后会发生什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:58.82,0:59:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know uh every every time I I stay up late at the lab the robots break doing something weird.\N你知道，每次我熬夜待在实验室，机器人就会莫名其妙地出问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.72,0:59:06.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm like ah so frustrated.\N我真是气死了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:06.42,0:59:10.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let me think about what's going to happen in 20 years and then I can carry on.\N让我想想二十年后会发生什么，然后我就能继续了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.27,0:59:10.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.84,0:59:19.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So 20 years from now, there are a couple of things that I'm super excited about that I think is just not that much uh far away.\N所以再过20年，有几件事让我非常兴奋，我觉得其实并不太远了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:19.19,0:59:22.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,One is uh robotics uh accelerating science, right?\N一个是机器人加速科学，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:22.83,0:59:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I have some friends in biomed and it's just so time consuming to do\N我有些生物医学领域的朋友，做一次实验耗时太长了，
Dialogue: 0,0:59:28.00,0:59:32.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,one experiment and so laborious like all those PhD students need to be in the lab,\N简直太费力了，所有那些博士生都得待在实验室里，
Dialogue: 0,0:59:33.01,0:59:33.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:33.41,0:59:35.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Attending to those like mouse, right?\N要照顾那些小鼠，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:35.77,0:59:39.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,All those like like you know dishes of of of cells.\N还有那些培养皿里的细胞。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.46,0:59:42.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,How about we automate all of that, right?\N那我们为什么不把所有这些都自动化呢，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:42.66,0:59:43.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Automating science.\N自动化科学。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:44.04,0:59:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then maybe all the medical research will not cost a billion dollars to do.\N那么也许所有的医学研究都不再需要花费十亿美元了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:48.16,0:59:54.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,They will be scaled up because we get this API to accelerate the physical world, right?\N因为我们有了这个API，可以加速物理世界的进步，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:54.87,0:59:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Using intelligence.\N利用智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.00,0:59:59.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perhaps that will be GR00T uh version 10 or something I hope.\N也许那就是 GR00T 的 10 版本之类的，我希望如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.31,0:59:59.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.64,1:00:01.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that is one thing I'm super excited about.\N所以这是我非常兴奋的一件事。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.74,1:00:05.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the other thing is robotics automating robotics itself.\N另一件事是，机器人正在自动化地自我制造。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:05.60,1:00:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.16,1:00:09.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So why don't we have robots fixing each other right?\N那为什么我们不能让机器人自己修理自己呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:09.81,1:00:16.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we see all of those big factories making the robots but how about the robots themselves assembling the next generation of the robots\N我们看到那些大型工厂在制造机器人，但机器人自己组装下一代机器人又如何呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:16.66,1:00:23.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,and I don't think this science fiction at all because actually in the LOM community again they are ahead of us unfortunately but in\N我觉得这完全不是科幻，因为在 LOM 社区中，他们实际上已经走在我们前面了，可惜的是。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:23.12,1:00:31.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,the LM community people are studying autoML meaning that can we prompt these LOMs to do deep research right to find the next best\N在 LM 社区中，人们正在研究自动机器学习，也就是我们能否引导这些 LOM 做深度研究，\N找到下一个最佳的变换器，找到智能本身的最佳架构。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:31.94,1:00:40.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,transformer to find the next best architecture for intelligence itself and people are actively doing this as we speak and probably OM is going to\N人们正在实时开展这项工作，而且很可能 OM 会率先解决这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:40.06,1:00:47.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,solve that first and then we're going to copy homework and we'll have the physical world doing this recursive self-improvement as we go and\N然后我们就能照搬作业，让物理世界实现这种递归的自我改进，而我们也将随之推进。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:47.31,1:00:53.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's going to happen right not in a 100 years only in 20 years that's definitely going to happen so I'm going\N我认为这不会在100年内发生，而是在20年内就一定会实现，所以我现在就结束。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:53.98,1:01:01.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,to end on a on a bright note I think we as a generation all of us were born too late to explore the\N我想以一个积极的基调结束，我们这一代人，所有人，出生得太晚，无法探索地球，
Dialogue: 0,1:01:01.26,1:01:05.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,earth were born too early to travel to other galaxies were born\N又出生得太早，无法前往其他星系，但刚好赶上，
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.42,1:01:14.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,just in time to solve robotics and everything that moves will be autonomous.\N解决机器人问题，所有会移动的东西都将实现自主。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.57,1:01:18.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,I love that.\N我喜欢这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:18.88,1:01:21.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, I think that's the best note to end on.\N我觉得这是最棒的收尾方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:21.98,1:01:29.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you all so much to to our panelists for for coming, sharing your thoughts, not only on where we are now, but where we are headed.\N非常感谢各位，感谢各位 panelist 前来参与，分享你们的见解，\N不仅关于我们现在所处的位置，也关于我们的未来方向。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:29.84,1:01:37.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just a note before everyone heads out, we aren't doing a traditional Q&A, but we are going to get remove our mics, come back here,\N在大家离开前提醒一下，我们不会进行传统的问答环节，但我们会取下麦克风，回到这里，
Dialogue: 0,1:01:37.18,1:01:46.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,and for anyone who's interested, feel free to come up to the stage and you can ask your questions directly to uh the panelists for anyone interested.\N任何有兴趣的人，都可以走上台来，直接向 panelist 们提问。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:46.24,1:01:48.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're just going to go off stage, get our mics removed.\N我们现在就下台，取下麦克风。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:48.44,1:01:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll be back for any questions.\N我们会回来回答问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.00,1:01:53.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Come up to the stage.\N请走上台来。
